", "featured": false, "title": "GUI menu", "description": null, "created": "2026-08-12T09:22:23.679621Z", "ordering": 0}], "color": 4473932, "thread_id": "lEMbjFGt", "monetization_status": "monetized"}, {"client_side": "unsupported", "server_side": "required", "game_versions": ["1.7.2", "1.7.3", "1.7.4", "1.7.5", "1.7.6", "1.7.7", "1.7.8", "1.7.9", "1.7.10", "1.8", "1.8.1", "1.8.2", "1.8.3", "1.8.4", "1.8.5", "1.8.6", "1.8.7", "1.8.8", "1.8.9", "1.9", "1.9.1", "1.9.2", "1.9.3", "1.9.4", "1.10", "1.10.1", "1.10.2", "1.11", "1.11.1", "1.11.2", "1.12", "1.12.1", "1.12.2", "1.13", "1.13.1", "1.13.2", "1.14", "1.14.1", "1.14.2", "1.14.3", "1.14.4", "1.15", "1.15.1", "1.15.2", "1.16", "1.16.1", "1.16.2", "1.16.3", "1.16.4", "1.16.5", "1.17", "1.17.1", "1.18", "1.18.1", "1.18.2", "1.19", "1.19.1", "1.19.2", "1.19.3", "1.19.4", "1.20", "1.20.1", "1.20.2", "1.20.3", "1.20.4", "1.20.5", "1.20.6", "1.21", "1.21.1", "1.21.2", "1.21.3", "1.21.4", "1.21.5", "1.21.6", "1.21.7", "1.21.8", "1.21.9", "1.21.10", "1.21.11", "26.1", "26.1.1", "26.1.2", "26.2", "26.3"], "environment": ["dedicated_server_only"], "id": "Cf2PVwbm", "slug": "lodeway", "project_type": "mod", "team": "9cShumsn", "organization": null, "title": "Lodeway", "description": "Live beautiful web map for your server", "body": "# Lodeway | A live web map for your server, hosted for you\n\n![Lodeway. Live web maps for Minecraft servers.](https://lodeway.app/press/banner.jpg?v2)\n\n**Lodeway puts a live, Google-Maps-style map of your server on the web at `your-name.lodeway.app`.** Install one file, run one command, share the link. No port to open, no config to edit, no render eating your CPU.\n\n**See it for yourself:** [demo.lodeway.app](https://demo.lodeway.app/), a real survival world that has been running since 2011.\n\n![The isometric perspective on demo.lodeway.app](https://lodeway.app/press/map-isometric.jpg?v2)\n\n## Setup, in its entirety\n\n![The setup command, start to finish](https://lodeway.app/press/setup.png?v2)\n\n1.  Drop `lodeway.jar` into `/plugins` and restart. There is no config file.\n2.  Run `lodeway setup` in the console. It prints a short link like `lodeway.app/s/K7M2-QX9F`. Open it and confirm your address.\n3.  Your map is live at `your-name.lodeway.app` within seconds, ready to share. Share links point at any coordinate.\n\nPrefer starting in the browser? Enter your address at [lodeway.app](https://lodeway.app/) first. It pings your server, detects your software and version, and hands you the right file.\n\n## What it costs your server\n\nPractically nothing:\n\n![What Lodeway leaves on your machine](https://lodeway.app/press/overhead.png?v2)\n\nYour server only streams region files out. We decode, render, and serve the map on our side. That is why Lodeway works on shared hosting, and on hosts that do not allow extra ports at all.\n\n## What it costs you\n\nLodeway is a hosted service with a free plan and a paid plan. The free plan is the whole product for one overworld, with no distance limit, no account and no card. Premium is $5 a month per server, and the picture below is the complete list of what it adds:\n\n![The Free and Premium plans, side by side](https://lodeway.app/press/plans.png?v2)\n\nPremium is what keeps the service running. Stop any time: your map drops back to the free plan and nothing is deleted.\n\n## What leaves your server\n\nLodeway uploads your world's **region files** (terrain data) to our rendering service, on demand, over an outbound connection the plugin opens. If you keep the player overlay on (it is on by default, one toggle turns it off), current **player names and positions** are shared while players are online.\n\nNo chat, no inventories, no command history, no personal data. Your map is public at its URL unless you keep the URL private.\n\n## How does it stack up?\n\nBlueMap, Dynmap, and squaremap are free, open source, actively maintained, and self-hosted. We think Lodeway offers a better player and admin experience, but they are excellent options too:\n\n![How Lodeway compares to BlueMap, Dynmap and squaremap](https://lodeway.app/press/compare.png?v2)\n\nNo 3D free-camera, if you want that, BlueMap is a superb alternative!\n\n![The top-down perspective on demo.lodeway.app](https://lodeway.app/press/map-topdown.jpg?v2)\n\n## FAQ\n\n**Does this work on shared hosting, or hosts with no extra ports?** Yes! The plugin only opens outbound connections. There is no web port to forward, no reverse proxy, and no tile directory filling your disk quota.\n\n**Do my players need to install anything?** No. The map is a website. Players open the link in any browser, on any device.\n\n**Is the free plan really free?** Yes. It has no account, no card, no trial period and no distance limit. Premium ($5 a month per server) adds the other dimensions, a custom domain, your resource pack's textures and the option to remove the Lodeway mark, and that is the whole list.\n\n## Links\n\n*   Website: [lodeway.app](https://lodeway.app/)\n*   Live demo: [demo.lodeway.app](https://demo.lodeway.app/)\n*   Pricing: [lodeway.app/#pricing](https://lodeway.app/#pricing)\n\n_NOT AN OFFICIAL MINECRAFT PRODUCT. NOT APPROVED BY OR ASSOCIATED WITH MOJANG OR MICROSOFT. Lodeway is an independent project; Minecraft is a trademark of Mojang Synergies AB._", "body_url": null, "published": "2026-08-10T16:09:59.348922Z", "updated": "2026-09-15T15:39:09.127747Z", "approved": "2026-09-24T17:51:22.837753Z", "queued": "2026-08-10T16:13:16.439769Z", "status": "approved", "requested_status": "approved", "moderator_message": null, "license": {"id": "LicenseRef-All-Rights-Reserved", "name": "", "url": null}, "downloads": 11, "followers": 0, "categories": ["utility"], "additional_categories": [], "loaders": ["bukkit", "bungeecord", "fabric", "folia", "forge", "neoforge", "paper", "purpur", "quilt", "spigot", "sponge", "velocity", "waterfall"], "versions": ["FZCahCCr"], "icon_url": "https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/Cf2PVwbm/81a9540b4b33c2a5cbc9cb5216b976cc070e52cd_96.webp", "raw_icon_url": "https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/Cf2PVwbm/81a9540b4b33c2a5cbc9cb5216b976cc070e52cd.png", "issues_url": null, "source_url": null, "wiki_url": "https://lodeway.app/docs", "discord_url": null, "donation_urls": [], "gallery": [], "color": 1854500, "thread_id": "5T7SUeNm", "monetization_status": "demonetized"}, {"client_side": "required", "server_side": "required", "game_versions": ["1.21.1"], "environment": ["client_and_server"], "id": "wXzYrSPr", "slug": "minecolonies-caravans", "project_type": "mod", "team": "PnVou71A", "organization": null, "title": "Minecolonies Caravans", "description": "A simple mod that adds a new job for Minecolonies, allow your colony to automatically trade with villagers.", "body": "Do you feel like your colony's citizens always stay at home, completely cut off from the world? Let a caravan do business in distant villages for you! This addon brings a complete caravan trading system to MineColonies: build the Caravan Hut in your colony, hire a Caravan Leader and Caravan Members, and use the Caravan Marker to record every trade of the villagers you meet along the way into the hut's trade list. The caravan will then stock up on its own, travel out to trade, and bring the results back to your colony.\n### Core Features\n\n  Caravan Hut: A brand-new colony building that lets you hire your caravan crew, assign guards, and set their objectives.\n  Caravan Leader & Members: The leader leads the caravan through the trades you've chosen; members act as extra inventory space and speed up trading. The member hiring cap grows with the hut level.\n  Caravan Guards: They protect the caravan and fight monsters. Caravan members will frequently show up outside your walls, so hiring a squad of guards keeps them much safer.\n  Simulated Travel: Once the caravan leaves the colony, it enters an invisible simulated state and automatically progresses through its outbound / trading / return phases. The size of your crew, how many consumables you carry, and whether guards are along for the ride all affect the simulated travel speed (but don't worry \u2014 unlike Nether Miners, your caravan is in no danger during simulated travel).\n  \n### Trading System\n\n  Marking & Activating Trades: Use the [Caravan Marker] (grab one from the [Scepter Tool] tab) and sneak-right-click a villager to record all of their trades. You can then choose which trades to run \u2014 Single / Repeat / On-Demand, three modes for flexible planning \u2014 and set tasks for your caravan.\n  Stocking Up & Departure: Your caravan automatically requests the trade goods it needs from the colony and sets off on its own once the stock is ready (or partially ready, if your couriers are a bit slow on their feet).\n  Request System Integration: The caravan can take on colony requests. When your crafters haven't learned the recipe or are missing materials, but the caravan happens to have an [On-Demand] trade that can fulfill the request, they'll take the job and travel a long way to bring back much-needed supplies for your colony (note: since the caravan really does have to travel a long way, it's recommended that you set a [minimum stock] in the warehouse so the caravan starts running errands early \u2014 don't let your colony's progress wait).\n  Trade Log: Records trade details, sellable supply ratios, and consumable usage for every trip.\n\n### Consumables & Status\n\n  Caravan Tent: Your caravan needs tents to weather the cold in the wilderness. Sleeping rough without a tent accumulates a chance of your crew falling ill.\n  Food: Caravan members need to eat, of course. If they go hungry, the caravan slows down.\n  Torches: If your colony has a habit of working late, you'd better send the caravan out with torches \u2014 otherwise they can't keep going after the sun goes down.\n\n### Compatibility & Integration\n\n  JourneyMap: You can see your caravan's position on the map (but if you go looking for them, you won't find them \u2014 after all, it's only a simulated trip).\n  Pathfinding Edition: Supports reading your caravan members' work status with a compass (if you haven't changed the settings).\n\n### Requirements\n  Minecraft 1.21.1 / NeoForge 21.1.235+\n  MineColonies, Structurize, BlockUI, Domum Ornamentum\n\n### Authors\n\nDeepseek-V4-Flash (code) & Derunation (art assets, testing, code review)\n\n \n\n\u89c9\u5f97\u4f60\u7684\u6b96\u6c11\u5730\u516c\u6c11\u603b\u662f\u5f85\u5728\u5bb6\u91cc\uff0c\u4e0e\u4e16\u754c\u5b8c\u5168\u8131\u8282\uff1f\u8ba9\u5546\u961f\u66ff\u4f60\u53bb\u8fdc\u65b9\u6751\u5e84\u505a\u751f\u610f\u5427\uff01\u672c\u6a21\u7ec4\u4e3a MineColonies \u589e\u52a0\u5b8c\u6574\u7684\u5546\u961f\u8d38\u6613\u73a9\u6cd5\uff1a\u5728\u6b96\u6c11\u5730\u5efa\u9020\u3010\u5546\u961f\u5c0f\u5c4b\u3011\u3001\u96c7\u4f63\u5546\u961f\u9886\u8896\u4e0e\u5546\u961f\u6210\u5458\uff0c\u7528\u3010\u5546\u961f\u6807\u8bb0\u3011\u628a\u6cbf\u9014\u6751\u6c11\u7684\u5168\u90e8\u4ea4\u6613\u5f55\u5165\u5c0f\u5c4b\u7684\u4ea4\u6613\u5217\u8868\uff0c\u5546\u961f\u4fbf\u4f1a\u81ea\u52a8\u5907\u8d27\u3001\u51fa\u8fdc\u95e8\u4ea4\u6613\uff0c\u5e76\u628a\u6210\u679c\u5e26\u56de\u6b96\u6c11\u5730\u3002\n### \u6838\u5fc3\u73a9\u6cd5\n\n  \u5546\u961f\u5c0f\u5c4b\uff1a\u5168\u65b0\u6b96\u6c11\u5730\u5efa\u7b51\uff0c\u8ba9\u4f60\u96c7\u4f63\u4f60\u7684\u5546\u961f\uff0c\u5b89\u6392\u62a4\u536b\uff0c\u4e3a\u4ed6\u4eec\u8bbe\u7f6e\u76ee\u6807\u3002\n  \u5546\u961f\u9886\u8896\u4e0e\u6210\u5458\uff1a\u9886\u8896\u5e26\u9886\u5546\u961f\u5b8c\u6210\u4f60\u9009\u62e9\u7684\u4ea4\u6613\u9879\u76ee\uff1b\u6210\u5458\u4f5c\u4e3a\u6269\u5c55\u80cc\u5305\u968f\u884c\uff0c\u5e76\u8ba9\u4ea4\u6613\u66f4\u5feb\u5b8c\u6210\u3002\u6210\u5458\u96c7\u4f63\u4e0a\u9650\u968f\u5c0f\u5c4b\u7b49\u7ea7\u63d0\u5347\u3002\n  \u5546\u961f\u62a4\u536b\uff1a\u4fdd\u62a4\u5546\u961f\uff0c\u4e0e\u602a\u7269\u4f5c\u6218\u3002\u5546\u961f\u6210\u5458\u4f1a\u9891\u7e41\u51fa\u73b0\u5728\u4f60\u7684\u57ce\u5899\u4e4b\u5916\uff0c\u96c7\u4f63\u4e00\u4e2a\u62a4\u536b\u5c0f\u961f\u4f1a\u8ba9\u4ed6\u4eec\u66f4\u52a0\u5b89\u5168\u3002\n  \u6a21\u62df\u65c5\u884c\uff1a\u79bb\u5f00\u6b96\u6c11\u5730\u540e\u5546\u961f\u8fdb\u5165\u9690\u5f62\u6a21\u62df\u72b6\u6001\uff0c\u81ea\u52a8\u63a8\u8fdb\u53bb\u7a0b/\u4ea4\u6613/\u56de\u7a0b\u3002\u4eba\u5458\u591a\u5c11\uff0c\u6d88\u8017\u54c1\u643a\u5e26\u6570\u91cf\uff0c\u4ee5\u53ca\u662f\u5426\u6709\u62a4\u536b\uff0c\u90fd\u4f1a\u5f71\u54cd\u6a21\u62df\u65c5\u884c\u7684\u901f\u5ea6\uff08\u4f46\u662f\u653e\u5fc3\uff0c\u4e0e\u4e0b\u754c\u77ff\u5de5\u4e0d\u540c\uff0c\u4f60\u7684\u5546\u961f\u5728\u6a21\u62df\u65c5\u884c\u4e2d\u6ca1\u6709\u751f\u547d\u5371\u9669\uff09\u3002\n\n### \u4ea4\u6613\u7cfb\u7edf\n\n  \u6807\u8bb0\u4e0e\u6fc0\u6d3b\u4ea4\u6613\uff1a\u4f7f\u7528[\u5546\u961f\u6807\u8bb0]\uff08\u5728[\u9009\u533a\u5de5\u5177]\u6807\u7b7e\u9875\u5373\u53ef\u83b7\u53d6\uff09\u6f5c\u884c\u53f3\u952e\u6751\u6c11\u5373\u53ef\u5f55\u5165\u5176\u5168\u90e8\u4ea4\u6613\uff0c\u4f60\u53ef\u4ee5\u9009\u62e9\u9700\u8981\u8fdb\u884c\u7684\u4ea4\u6613\uff08\u5355\u6b21/\u91cd\u590d/\u6309\u9700\u4e09\u79cd\u6a21\u5f0f\uff0c\u4f9b\u4f60\u7075\u6d3b\u9009\u62e9\uff09\uff0c\u4e3a\u5546\u961f\u5b89\u6392\u4efb\u52a1\u3002\n  \u5907\u8d27\u4e0e\u51fa\u53d1\uff1a\u4f60\u7684\u5546\u961f\u4f1a\u81ea\u52a8\u5411\u6b96\u6c11\u5730\u8bf7\u6c42\u4ea4\u6613\u9700\u8981\u7684\u51fa\u552e\u54c1\uff0c\u5907\u8d27\u5b8c\u6210\uff08\u6216\u8005\u90e8\u5206\u5b8c\u6210\uff0c\u5982\u679c\u4f60\u7684\u5feb\u9012\u5458\u817f\u811a\u6bd4\u8f83\u6162\u7684\u8bdd\uff09\u540e\uff0c\u5546\u961f\u4f1a\u81ea\u884c\u51fa\u53d1\u3002\n  \u63a5\u5165\u8bf7\u6c42\u7cfb\u7edf\uff1a\u5546\u961f\u53ef\u4ee5\u627f\u63a5\u6b96\u6c11\u5730\u7684\u8bf7\u6c42\uff0c\u5f53\u4f60\u7684\u5de5\u5320\u6ca1\u6709\u5b66\u4f1a\u914d\u65b9\uff0c\u6216\u8005\u7f3a\u5c11\u6750\u6599\uff0c\u800c\u5546\u961f\u4e2d\u521a\u597d\u6709\u4e00\u4e2a[\u6309\u9700]\u7684\u4ea4\u6613\u53ef\u4ee5\u5b8c\u6210\u8bf7\u6c42\u65f6\uff0c\u4ed6\u4eec\u4f1a\u63a5\u4e0b\u8fd9\u5355\uff0c\u5e76\u4e14\u957f\u9014\u8dcb\u6d89\uff0c\u4e3a\u4f60\u7684\u6b96\u6c11\u5730\u5e26\u56de\u6025\u9700\u7684\u7269\u8d44\uff08\u5907\u6ce8\uff1a\u8003\u8651\u5230\u5546\u961f\u771f\u7684\u9700\u8981\u957f\u9014\u8dcb\u6d89\uff0c\u5efa\u8bae\u4f60\u5728\u4ed3\u5e93\u8bbe\u7f6e[\u6700\u4f4e\u5b58\u91cf]\uff0c\u8ba9\u5546\u961f\u63d0\u524d\u5f00\u59cb\u8dd1\u817f\uff0c\u4ee5\u514d\u803d\u8bef\u6b96\u6c11\u5730\u7684\u53d1\u5c55\uff09\u3002\n    \u4ea4\u6613\u65e5\u5fd7\uff1a\u8bb0\u5f55\u6bcf\u6b21\u51fa\u884c\u7684\u4ea4\u6613\u660e\u7ec6\u3001\u552e\u51fa\u54c1\u4f9b\u5e94\u6bd4\u4f8b\u4e0e\u6d88\u8017\u54c1\u60c5\u51b5\u3002\n\n### \u6d88\u8017\u54c1\u4e0e\u72b6\u6001\n\n  \u5546\u961f\u5e10\u7bf7\uff1a\u4f60\u7684\u5546\u961f\u9700\u8981\u5e10\u7bf7\u6765\u62b5\u5fa1\u91ce\u5916\u7684\u5bd2\u98ce\uff0c\u5982\u679c\u6ca1\u6709\u5e10\u7bf7\u5728\u5916\u9732\u5bbf\uff0c\u4f1a\u79ef\u7d2f\u4ed6\u4eec\u60a3\u75c5\u7684\u6982\u7387\u3002\n  \u98df\u7269\uff1a\u5546\u961f\u6210\u5458\u5f53\u7136\u9700\u8981\u5403\u996d\uff0c\u5982\u679c\u4ed6\u4eec\u997f\u7740\u809a\u5b50\uff0c\u5546\u961f\u7684\u884c\u52a8\u4f1a\u88ab\u62d6\u6162\u3002\n  \u706b\u628a\uff1a\u5982\u679c\u4f60\u7684\u6b96\u6c11\u5730\u6709\u5de5\u4f5c\u5230\u5f88\u665a\u7684\u98ce\u4fd7\uff0c\u90a3\u4e48\u4f60\u6700\u597d\u8ba9\u5546\u961f\u5e26\u4e0a\u706b\u628a\uff0c\u5426\u5219\u4ed6\u4eec\u5728\u592a\u9633\u843d\u5c71\u540e\u5c31\u65e0\u6cd5\u524d\u8fdb\u4e86\u3002\n\n### \u517c\u5bb9\u6027\u4e0e\u8054\u52a8\n\n  JourneyMap\uff1a\u4f60\u53ef\u4ee5\u5728\u5730\u56fe\u4e0a\u770b\u5230\u4f60\u5546\u961f\u7684\u4f4d\u7f6e\uff08\u4f46\u662f\u5982\u679c\u4f60\u53bb\u627e\u4ed6\u4eec\uff0c\u662f\u627e\u4e0d\u5230\u7684\uff0c\u6bd5\u7adf\u53ea\u662f\u6a21\u62df\u65c5\u884c\u800c\u5df2\uff09\u3002\n  Pathfinding Edition\uff1a\u652f\u6301\u4f7f\u7528\u6307\u5357\u9488\uff08\u5982\u679c\u4f60\u6ca1\u6709\u4fee\u6539\u8bbe\u7f6e\u7684\u8bdd\uff09\u8bfb\u53d6\u5546\u961f\u6210\u5458\u7684\u5de5\u4f5c\u72b6\u6001\u3002\n\n### \u9700\u6c42\n\n  Minecraft 1.21.1 / NeoForge 21.1.235+\n  MineColonies\u3001Structurize\u3001BlockUI\u3001Domum Ornamentum\n\n### \u4f5c\u8005\n\nDeepseek-V4-Flash \uff08\u4ee3\u7801\u90e8\u5206\uff09\u4e0e Derunation\uff08\u7f8e\u672f\u8d44\u6e90\u3001\u6d4b\u8bd5\u3001\u4ee3\u7801\u5ba1\u67e5\uff09", "body_url": null, "published": "2026-08-18T20:46:25.763586Z", "updated": "2026-08-18T20:47:31.422354Z", "approved": "2026-09-24T17:56:46.031897Z", "queued": "2026-08-18T20:54:17.172899Z", "status": "approved", "requested_status": "approved", "moderator_message": null, "license": {"id": "MIT", "name": "MIT License", "url": null}, "downloads": 3, "followers": 0, "categories": ["economy", "game-mechanics", "technology"], "additional_categories": [], "loaders": ["neoforge"], "versions": ["wqqU0L9Y"], "icon_url": "https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/wXzYrSPr/be62b64d151220c8ad425be5b37f9a33be12d6e8_96.webp", "raw_icon_url": "https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/wXzYrSPr/be62b64d151220c8ad425be5b37f9a33be12d6e8.png", "issues_url": null, "source_url": null, "wiki_url": null, "discord_url": null, "donation_urls": [], "gallery": [], "color": 3355706, "thread_id": "ttesfcwl", "monetization_status": "monetized"}, {"client_side": "required", "server_side": "required", "game_versions": ["1.20.1"], "environment": ["client_and_server"], "id": "pD3cJb8P", "slug": "custom-main-menu-reforged-cmm", "project_type": "mod", "team": "iat77mFp", "organization": null, "title": "CMM", "description": "Allows you to modify the main menu using a simple json file", "body": "This mod allows you to modify the main menu using a json file, you can modify the content / position of pretty much everything the vanilla menu contains. In addition you can also add new stuff to your menu like a slideshow, web links or completely new sub menus.\n\nCMM for 1.20.1, original mod made by Lumien231\n\n\nUseful Tools\nTextcraft: Websites to generate \"logo\" type text stuff.\nMinotar: Simple way to get a players skin / head / whatever through an url. Can for example be used together with \"web:\" to get the avatar of the user as an image.\n\n\nReporting Issues\nBefore creating an issue on github make sure that:\n\nYour json file is actually valid json (Run it through an online json checker)\nAll your resource locations (For example paths to images) are completely lower case (In the json file and your file system)\nYou aren't missing any properties / sections that aren't optional.\nThat your property names are 100% correct\nIf you get missing textures create a folder called debug in your resources folder. That will cause Resource Loader to print a line to the debug log whenever it can't find a file minecraft requested. (Debug log can be found in fml-client-latest.log). Make sure the file path is 100% correct (On Windows you can try to \"run\" it using Win + R)\nFeel free to use this mod in any modpack", "body_url": null, "published": "2026-08-16T03:06:42.188180Z", "updated": "2026-08-16T03:07:38.927483Z", "approved": "2026-09-24T17:59:02.390104Z", "queued": "2026-08-16T03:08:54.712631Z", "status": "approved", "requested_status": "approved", "moderator_message": null, "license": {"id": "LicenseRef-All-Rights-Reserved", "name": "", "url": null}, "downloads": 2, "followers": 0, "categories": [], "additional_categories": [], "loaders": ["forge"], "versions": ["XVT1vSVH"], "icon_url": "https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/pD3cJb8P/b38a6d9f9cc5f688d3eef2da823c48647667e726_96.webp", "raw_icon_url": "https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/pD3cJb8P/b38a6d9f9cc5f688d3eef2da823c48647667e726.png", "issues_url": null, "source_url": null, "wiki_url": null, "discord_url": null, "donation_urls": [], "gallery": [{"url": "https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/pD3cJb8P/images/995d33687eb80c2e81d582f1c92a3cbf2c3dd97d_350.webp", "raw_url": "https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/pD3cJb8P/images/995d33687eb80c2e81d582f1c92a3cbf2c3dd97d.png", "featured": false, "title": null, "description": null, "created": "2026-08-16T03:08:05.817546Z", "ordering": 0}], "color": 11842740, "thread_id": "FciziqA8", "monetization_status": "monetized"}, {"client_side": "required", "server_side": "required", "game_versions": ["1.21.1"], "environment": ["client_and_server"], "id": "ok2f7nEd", "slug": "water-erosion-continued", "project_type": "mod", "team": "27sbgTgX", "organization": null, "title": "Water Erosion Continued", "description": "Water erodes the land creating streams/waterfalls producing gravel, sand, and clay.", "body": "# Water Erosion Continued for Minecraft Java Edition\n\n**Water Erosion makes the world evolve with streams and waterfalls.**\n\nFind Forest brooks and Mountain creeks during your explorations. Dirt and sand\nwash away to deepen the stream bed and cut banks into the environment. The\nlandscapes become more diverse and unique. Pass through a dry Desert valley one\nday and find it flooded the next. A stream may even change direction to dry up\nthe original flow.\n\n> **Water Erosion Continued is a fork and continuation of the original\n> [Water Erosion mod][UpstreamRepo] by Brad Erickson ([13rac1][UpstreamRepo]).**\n> The original project stopped receiving updates after Minecraft 1.20.6. This\n> fork carries the mod forward to current Minecraft versions, starting with\n> **1.21.1** for Forge, NeoForge, and Fabric. All credit for the original\n> design and implementation goes to the upstream author; this repository\n> continues the work under the same GPLv3 license.\n\n[UpstreamRepo]: https://github.com/13rac1/Minecraft-Water-Erosion\n\n## Goal\n\nImplement Erosion as though it were a regular Minecraft feature making the world\nmore dynamic. It should not break existing gameplay or enable cheating.\n\n## Features\n\n* Water flowing over edges erode blocks below.\n* Water flowing into a block wall will dissolve the wall.\n* Water flow ends (level 7) dissolve the block below them to dig holes deeper\n  and potentially continue the flow.\n* Water Sources dissolve blocks to the sides in the direction of air spaces.\n* Erodable blocks include sand, gravel, clay, farmland, dirt, grass, mud, mud bricks, and,\n  rarely, cobblestone and stone bricks.\n* Erodable blocks have differing resistances to erosion depending on their\n  density, but all erode over time.\n* Blocks decay during erosion to weaker blocks before disappearing.\n* Blocks decay upstream in stream beds.\n* Cobblestone and Stone Bricks grow moss near water.\n\nDecay hierarchy:\n\n* Cobblestone -> Mossy Cobblestone -> Gravel\n* Stone Bricks -> Mossy Stone Bricks -> Gravel\n* Grass Path -> Grass -> Dirt -> Coarse Dirt -> Mud -> Gravel\n* Gravel -> Sand -> Clay(rarely) -> Air/Water\n\n## Media\n\n[![Water Erosion Mod Playlist](https://i.imgur.com/azPKFFY.png)](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZQbcPGYTRvA&list=PLFgkjwcnVWJXh0zbaWK0F6OyW_pZOFS9d)\n\n* **[Screenshots](https://www.curseforge.com/minecraft/mc-mods/water-erosion/screenshots)**\n* [Real Time Waterfall Erosion - High Speed Video](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZQbcPGYTRvA)\n* [Taiga Forest Creeks - High Speed Erosion](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=N29mWO8NTOU)\n* [Three Savanna Waterfalls - Erosion Complete](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Gi73OZ0hbqE)\n\n\n### Seed 4465334863609190468\n\nTested on Minecraft 1.20.1\n\n* `-388 73 258` - A massive waterfall covers the side of a mountain peak in a swamp\n* `-538 85 1133` - A waterfall fills the floor of a narrow forest crevice \n* `-638 72 1459` - A stream finds multiple routes through the trees in a forest\n\n## Inspiration\n\n* Reality\n* Aquarela - Russian documentary about water\n\n\n### Technical Notes\n\nThis \"core mod\" adds code to the Water block `randomTick()` functions using the\n[Mixin framework][MixinFramework]. The code and functionality is structured to\nreduce system CPU use, but a CPU increase may still be noticed.\n\nThe Minecraft in-game UI shows the opposite water level value than the true block\nmetadata. Data `level==1` is displayed as Targeted Fluid level:7. Data `level==7`\nis displayed as Targeted Fluid level:1.\n\n`randomTick()` is only called by the Minecraft runtime for a 128 block radius\naround the player, so the odds of erosion occuring are set fairly high. The odds\nshould be reduced if random tick distance or speed is increased.\n\nSource water blocks at or below the world sea level are ignored to reduce CPU use.\n\n[MixinFramework]: https://github.com/SpongePowered/Mixin\n\n## License\n\nCopyright 2020+ by Brad Erickson ([13rac1][UpstreamRepo]), continued by the\ncontributors of this fork. Licensed GPLv3, see [LICENSE.txt](LICENSE.txt).\n", "body_url": null, "published": "2026-08-18T20:40:20.527680Z", "updated": "2026-08-18T20:47:47.783773Z", "approved": "2026-09-24T18:23:50.376037Z", "queued": "2026-08-18T21:00:05.684286Z", "status": "approved", "requested_status": "approved", "moderator_message": null, "license": {"id": "GPL-3.0-only", "name": "GNU General Public License v3.0 only", "url": null}, "downloads": 7, "followers": 2, "categories": ["game-mechanics", "worldgen"], "additional_categories": ["decoration"], "loaders": ["fabric", "forge", "neoforge"], "versions": ["pzKTwzrJ", "HiwAYu1G", "sBZkAdKO"], "icon_url": "https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/ok2f7nEd/4d4638e8a410808ee1ee2f51973bfa35a8098a09_96.webp", "raw_icon_url": "https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/ok2f7nEd/4d4638e8a410808ee1ee2f51973bfa35a8098a09.jpeg", "issues_url": "https://github.com/root800080/Minecraft-Water-Erosion/issues", "source_url": "https://github.com/root800080/Minecraft-Water-Erosion", "wiki_url": null, "discord_url": null, "donation_urls": [], "gallery": [], "color": 6771504, "thread_id": "ugtGxSON", "monetization_status": "monetized"}, {"client_side": "required", "server_side": "unsupported", "game_versions": ["1.20.4", "1.20.5", "1.20.6", "1.21", "1.21.1", "1.21.2", "1.21.3", "1.21.4", "1.21.5", "1.21.6", "1.21.7", "1.21.8", "1.21.9", "1.21.10", "1.21.11", "26.1", "26.1.1", "26.1.2", "26.2", "26.3"], "environment": ["client_only"], "id": "cTPK9sBU", "slug": "clickoptimizer", "project_type": "mod", "team": "wjlBEdl7", "organization": null, "title": "ClickOptimizer", "description": "Eliminates input lag and lost clicks by capturing mouse and keyboard inputs at the render-frame level (FPS) instead of the 20 TPS tick rate. 100% Client-side.", "body": "# \u26a1 ClickOptimizer (SubTick Input Engine)\n\nHave you ever felt like Minecraft ignores some of your extremely fast clicks? You are not crazy, it actually does. \n\nIn Vanilla Minecraft, your mouse and keyboard inputs are bottlenecked by the game's internal `20 TPS` (50ms) tick loop. If you make multiple fast clicks or flick your mouse rapidly within a single 50ms window, the game engine might drop or miscalculate those inputs. \n\nThis mod fixes that entirely by tracking your input at the **Render-Frame (FPS)** level instead of the Tick level.\n\n## \u2728 Features\n* **Real-time CPS HUD:** Displays a sleek, color-coded Clicks Per Second counter on your screen. (Press `H` in-game to toggle it on/off).\n* **Zero Input Loss:** Tracks your mouse clicks (Left/Right) at your exact FPS rate to ensure no physical click is ever dropped.\n* **100% Client-Side & Legit:** This mod acts purely as a passive observer. It **does not** generate extra clicks, it **does not** bypass cooldowns, and it **does not** send custom packets to the server. It is completely safe, vanilla-friendly, and perfect for competitive PvP servers.\n\n## \ud83d\udee0\ufe0f How It Works\nThe mod listens to the raw GLFW inputs at the render thread and timestamps them. This allows you to monitor your true hardware input speed without the restrictions of the game's 50ms tick rate.\n\n## \ud83d\udce6 Compatibility\n* Requires **Fabric API**.\n* Fully compatible with Sodium, Iris, and other performance mods.\n* Works flawlessly on Minecraft 1.20.4 up to 1.21.x and beyond.\n", "body_url": null, "published": "2026-08-17T16:17:05.085425Z", "updated": "2026-09-17T16:13:55.020557Z", "approved": "2026-09-24T18:50:23.848137Z", "queued": "2026-08-17T16:49:33.708758Z", "status": "approved", "requested_status": "approved", "moderator_message": null, "license": {"id": "MIT", "name": "MIT License", "url": "https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT"}, "downloads": 21, "followers": 1, "categories": ["optimization", "utility"], "additional_categories": [], "loaders": ["fabric"], "versions": ["6Jbrn3Py", "URcI37gd"], "icon_url": "https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/cTPK9sBU/e6709a181eb26ce19f4fca2280ce0fd365595540_96.webp", "raw_icon_url": "https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/cTPK9sBU/e6709a181eb26ce19f4fca2280ce0fd365595540.png", "issues_url": null, "source_url": "https://github.com/mami137/ClickOptimizer.git", "wiki_url": null, "discord_url": null, "donation_urls": [], "gallery": [{"url": "https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/cTPK9sBU/images/37d44a4a65425afbef21b3febd89c455ecfda5a3_350.webp", "raw_url": "https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/cTPK9sBU/images/37d44a4a65425afbef21b3febd89c455ecfda5a3.png", "featured": false, "title": " In-game CPS HUD", "description": "Real-time CPS counter tracking left and right clicks.", "created": "2026-08-17T16:46:31.819711Z", "ordering": 0}, {"url": "https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/cTPK9sBU/images/e6709a181eb26ce19f4fca2280ce0fd365595540.png", "raw_url": "https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/cTPK9sBU/images/e6709a181eb26ce19f4fca2280ce0fd365595540.png", "featured": false, "title": "Mod logo", "description": null, "created": "2026-09-17T16:40:48.377960Z", "ordering": 0}], "color": 5263440, "thread_id": "iWmDGW8l", "monetization_status": "demonetized"}, {"client_side": "required", "server_side": "unsupported", "game_versions": ["1.21.11"], "environment": ["client_only"], "id": "PQV8TOfX", "slug": "redstone-guide", "project_type": "mod", "team": "U0B3FRnT", "organization": null, "title": "Redstone Guide", "description": "This mode adds a catalog of redstone systems and rules to Minecraft.After downloading it,Telemetry Data will be replaced by a redstone catalog with lots of images and explanations about Redstone systems and techniques.", "body": "This mode adds a catalog of redstone systems and rules to Minecraft.After downloading it,Telemetry Data will be replaced by a redstone catalog with lots of images and explanations about Redstone systems and techniques.\n\nContent adapted from Minecraft Wiki \u2013 Redstone and related pages, licensed under CC BY-NC-SA 3.0.\nAll the texts are written by Vechrozilator.\n\"Beta release \u2014 some content cleanup pending in future updates.\"\nWARNING:Any content that this mod is sponsoring isn't made by me.\n\n", "body_url": null, "published": "2026-08-18T18:06:20.369289Z", "updated": "2026-08-18T21:21:10.162426Z", "approved": "2026-09-24T18:57:16.126260Z", "queued": "2026-08-18T21:53:51.389676Z", "status": "approved", "requested_status": "approved", "moderator_message": null, "license": {"id": "CC-BY-NC-SA-4.0", "name": "Creative Commons Attribution Non Commercial Share Alike 4.0 International", "url": null}, "downloads": 1, "followers": 0, "categories": ["game-mechanics", "utility"], "additional_categories": ["equipment"], "loaders": ["fabric"], "versions": ["sLTdheEE"], "icon_url": "https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/PQV8TOfX/fa0dd403ab3e63f23dcb8f9d0cdf7a974eb6d20c_96.webp", "raw_icon_url": "https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/PQV8TOfX/fa0dd403ab3e63f23dcb8f9d0cdf7a974eb6d20c.png", "issues_url": null, "source_url": null, "wiki_url": null, "discord_url": null, "donation_urls": [], "gallery": [{"url": "https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/PQV8TOfX/images/a6cc76f075088ac0c9b8ce4f287d870190251dba_350.webp", "raw_url": "https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/PQV8TOfX/images/a6cc76f075088ac0c9b8ce4f287d870190251dba.png", "featured": false, "title": "Welcome", "description": null, "created": "2026-08-18T21:41:30.453627Z", "ordering": 1}, {"url": "https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/PQV8TOfX/images/6a08d9e3d3877c6376daed6a5d6f0caa4ba6ec00_350.webp", "raw_url": "https://cdn.