 \u00b7 ATiers \u00b7 MyTiers \u00b7 Central Tier List\n\n### Internet mode\n\nWhen enabled, TierLookup may send player names or identifiers to the selected tier-list services to retrieve tier data.\n\n### Installation\n\nRequires:\n\n* Minecraft `1.21.11`\n* Fabric Loader\n* Fabric API\n* Java 21\n\nMod Menu is optional, but recommended for settings.\n\nTierLookup is fully client-side \u2014 servers don't need to install anything.\n\n**Made by Lebushe**\n", "body_url": null, "published": "2026-08-19T00:59:24.787477Z", "updated": "2026-08-19T01:16:28.269537Z", "approved": "2026-09-24T19:21:01.443408Z", "queued": "2026-08-19T02:30:18.064142Z", "status": "approved", "requested_status": "approved", "moderator_message": null, "license": {"id": "LicenseRef-All-Rights-Reserved", "name": "", "url": null}, "downloads": 0, "followers": 0, "categories": ["utility"], "additional_categories": ["management", "social"], "loaders": ["fabric"], "versions": ["ghsRGV0A"], "icon_url": "https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/kJf4KXzO/52da94eabd0e3ff4ef7f1c6a03122b2e54fe3721_96.webp", "raw_icon_url": "https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/kJf4KXzO/52da94eabd0e3ff4ef7f1c6a03122b2e54fe3721.jpeg", "issues_url": "https://github.com/le6ush/TierLookup/issues", "source_url": "https://github.com/le6ush/TierLookup", "wiki_url": null, "discord_url": "https://discord.gg/GJZePCBmuH", "donation_urls": [], "gallery": [{"url": "https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/kJf4KXzO/images/6e7f9f0ca857359313fe568a7b36690fd09ebb8d_350.webp", "raw_url": "https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/kJf4KXzO/images/6e7f9f0ca857359313fe568a7b36690fd09ebb8d.png", "featured": false, "title": "TAB", "description": "Tiers directly in the player list.", "created": "2026-08-19T02:30:00.205623Z", "ordering": 1}, {"url": "https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/kJf4KXzO/images/27c1938e85263f95d5144b889b26fa168bf47c47.jpeg", "raw_url": "https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/kJf4KXzO/images/27c1938e85263f95d5144b889b26fa168bf47c47.jpeg", "featured": false, "title": "Quick Lookup", "description": "See tiers while looking at a player.", "created": "2026-08-19T02:29:35.099955Z", "ordering": 2}, {"url": "https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/kJf4KXzO/images/2a6f30285589dfd665b11db61063f50316a437f2.jpeg", "raw_url": "https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/kJf4KXzO/images/2a6f30285589dfd665b11db61063f50316a437f2.jpeg", "featured": true, "title": "Player Tiers", "description": "View a player's tiers and notes.", "created": "2026-08-19T02:29:08.763328Z", "ordering": 3}, {"url": "https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/kJf4KXzO/images/8988761b9d27d886087c2c07c5bb2e7a04ce9fe9.jpeg", "raw_url": "https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/kJf4KXzO/images/8988761b9d27d886087c2c07c5bb2e7a04ce9fe9.jpeg", "featured": false, "title": "Player Search", "description": "Search and favorite players.", "created": "2026-08-19T02:28:38.431441Z", "ordering": 4}], "color": 1776940, "thread_id": "TRtIBmvK", "monetization_status": "monetized"}, {"client_side": "required", "server_side": "unsupported", "game_versions": ["1.21.11", "26.1.2", "26.2"], "environment": ["client_only"], "id": "xsHqamix", "slug": "wtzos-cpvp-tweaks", "project_type": "mod", "team": "kONK8eJW", "organization": null, "title": "Wtzo's Cpvp Tweaks", "description": "This mod gives you tweaks for your gameplay to make you better.", "body": "Wtzo's Cpvp Tweaks\n\nWtzo's Cpvp Tweaks is a lightweight client-side Fabric mod focused on cleaner crystal PvP visibility and customizable first-person visuals. \n\n## Features\n\n- Brightness boost with an adjustable strength slider\n- Cleaner night vision rendering\n- Toggleable pumpkin blur\n- Adjustable fire height\n- Adjustable shield position\n- Separate first-person size controls for totems, crystals, golden apples, food, potions, ender pearls, rockets, buckets and shields\n- Hide the totem pop animation\n- Hide totem particles\n- Adjustable totem pop size\n- Hide explosion particles for clearer crystal PvP\n- Adjustable end crystal size without changing the crystal hitbox\n- Blindness, darkness, lava, powder snow, water and atmospheric fog controls\n- Keep maps visible while riding a boat\n- Fix shield rendering while using Riptide\n- Settings saved automatically in `config/wtzo.json`\n- Optional Mod Menu integration\n\n## Compatibility\n\n- Fabric Loader required\n- Java 25 for Minecraft 26.2\n- Mod Menu is optional\n- Client-side only\n\n\nOpen WTZO Tweaks through Mod Menu. Without Mod Menu, the settings button is available from Minecraft's Credits screen.\n", "body_url": null, "published": "2026-08-17T18:33:49.915183Z", "updated": "2026-08-21T18:46:03.357740Z", "approved": "2026-09-24T19:46:58.884504Z", "queued": "2026-08-17T19:00:26.730673Z", "status": "approved", "requested_status": "approved", "moderator_message": null, "license": {"id": "CC-BY-ND-4.0", "name": "Creative Commons Attribution No Derivatives 4.0 International", "url": null}, "downloads": 4, "followers": 0, "categories": [], "additional_categories": [], "loaders": ["fabric"], "versions": ["UYoEW9Td", "T8oIgNNm", "LlwgYvbe"], "icon_url": "https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/xsHqamix/336b277d8430c73379237f3fdb4712785052b13b_96.webp", "raw_icon_url": "https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/xsHqamix/336b277d8430c73379237f3fdb4712785052b13b.png", "issues_url": null, "source_url": null, "wiki_url": null, "discord_url": null, "donation_urls": [], "gallery": [{"url": "https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/xsHqamix/images/f83438755c82a1d8b0e44add84b844e903a71273_350.webp", "raw_url": "https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/xsHqamix/images/f83438755c82a1d8b0e44add84b844e903a71273.png", "featured": false, "title": "Modules", "description": "Heres the picture of the gui", "created": "2026-08-17T19:02:03.211027Z", "ordering": 0}], "color": 4272164, "thread_id": "5yS9Zyl7", "monetization_status": "monetized"}, {"client_side": "required", "server_side": "required", "game_versions": ["b1.7.3"], "environment": ["client_and_server"], "id": "TnSOUQrC", "slug": "coolbelt", "project_type": "mod", "team": "BKthUfpC", "organization": null, "title": "Coolbelt", "description": "Adds slots for your sword, pickaxe, axe, and shovel. Automatically switches between them.", "body": "![A screenshot showcasing several features of Coolbelt, namely the slots and the durability previews.](https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/TnSOUQrC/images/22c5a92bbaa6dfe403e8863c473c309971be2536.png)\n\n# Coolbelt\n\nCoolbelt is a toolbelt mod for Minecraft Beta 1.7.3 that adds slots for your **sword**, **pickaxe**, **axe**, and **shovel**. \nThe tool that is currently in-use is displayed in your main hand and replaces the item currently being held.\nThe mod automatically selects the most efficient tool for the job, and allows you to choose from several options for deciding which tool to use when the selected item is also a tool.\n\n## Dependencies\n\nThis mod requires the following in order to function:\n\n- [Babric](https://github.com/babric/prism-instance)\n- [Accessory API `>=0.8.1`](https://modrinth.com/mod/K9k9gNxR)\n- Optionally, to access Coolbelt's and Accessory API's options:\n  - [Glass Config API](https://modrinth.com/mod/rFeWTq4G)\n  - [Mod Menu Babric](https://modrinth.com/mod/vf3X9pHM)\n\n## Installation\n\n1. Ensure **Babric** and **Accessory API** are installed for Minecraft Beta 1.7.3.\n2. Download the `coolbelt-x.x.x.jar` file.\n3. Place the `.jar` file into your instance's `mods` directory.\n4. Launch the instance.\n\n## Compatibility\n\nMixes into `PlayerInventory`, `TextureManager`, `InGameHud`, `GameOptions`. `TranslationStorage`, `ToolItem`, `AxeItem`, `PickaxeItem`, `ShovelItem`, `SwordItem`.\n\n### Known Issues\n\nThe controls menu gets crowded when other mods also add keybinds.\\\n**Solution:** Install a mod that implements a scrollable controls screen.\n\nWith Accessory API versions lower than `0.9.0`, some HUD elements list items incorrectly.\\\n**Solution:** Upgrade to a newer version, or disable \"Always show tool durabilities\".\n\nInventory operations from other mods are offset by the amount of slots added to Accessory API.\\\n**Solution:** Check if the affected mod offers a compatibility patch or option.\n", "body_url": null, "published": "2026-08-18T20:45:46.300462Z", "updated": "2026-09-24T08:36:53.014732Z", "approved": "2026-09-24T17:51:19.773393Z", "queued": "2026-08-18T20:53:39.522433Z", "status": "approved", "requested_status": "approved", "moderator_message": null, "license": {"id": "MIT", "name": "MIT License", "url": null}, "downloads": 11, "followers": 1, "categories": ["utility"], "additional_categories": ["equipment"], "loaders": ["babric", "fabric"], "versions": ["4TOwotOY", "vjww9dAQ", "3qED4KGT", "276Bettk", "DsZB0HY0", "S8wCtcDi", "Q5KWy842", "bBzQk1qx", "KqyLLgEn", "3fDsEfwj", "E1Rn8BBm", "nUYjCJBt", "nWNmRkJP", "Yc6fEjd2", "2llduxXW", "W2647iA1", "I4ICQw7D", "RYHkMoVQ", "qVDxYstk", "G2WyVtIr", "85JwfTa8", "AyIZkoZp", "ZMqJI2wh", "6ZiKQ3pr", "Vt7eWbvj", "FpkXgq9L"], "icon_url": "https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/TnSOUQrC/3b1e72c01921ff766c7badac26c54e591d7bfe1a.png", "raw_icon_url": "https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/TnSOUQrC/3b1e72c01921ff766c7badac26c54e591d7bfe1a.png", "issues_url": "https://github.com/vanapiton/coolbelt/issues", "source_url": "https://github.com/vanapiton/coolbelt", "wiki_url": null, "discord_url": null, "donation_urls": [], "gallery": [{"url": "https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/TnSOUQrC/images/22c5a92bbaa6dfe403e8863c473c309971be2536_350.webp", "raw_url": "https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/TnSOUQrC/images/22c5a92bbaa6dfe403e8863c473c309971be2536.png", "featured": true, "title": "Showcase", "description": "A screenshot showcasing several features of the mod, namely the slots and the durability previews.", "created": "2026-09-11T00:20:13.075734Z", "ordering": 0}, {"url": "https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/TnSOUQrC/images/919dcf0979f0169d3fc3c0ef448b9e40720a4e33.png", "raw_url": "https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/TnSOUQrC/images/919dcf0979f0169d3fc3c0ef448b9e40720a4e33.png", "featured": false, "title": "Coolbelt Icon", "description": null, "created": "2026-09-07T10:03:12.711221Z", "ordering": 0}], "color": 3288417, "thread_id": "ue6MSYQe", "monetization_status": "monetized"}, {"client_side": "required", "server_side": "required", "game_versions": ["1.20.1"], "environment": ["client_and_server"], "id": "mEFIrXVS", "slug": "verity-mimottsasr", "project_type": "mod", "team": "R95xcMQ4", "organization": null, "title": "Verity MimoTTS/ASR", "description": "An unofficial mod that add Xiaomi mimo as Verity's TTS and ASR provider. (compatible with Smiley's better voice)", "body": "Give Verity a voice powered by Xiaomi MiMo.\nA pair of Forge addons that plug Xiaomi MiMo TTS & ASR into Verity JE (1.20.1) \u2014 Your Verity can now speak and understand Chinese (and English) through MiMo's API.\nTwo versions, pick one:\n|Version|Requires|Where settings live:\n|---|---|---\n|Addon|Verity + Smiley's Better Voice|its own config screen\n|Direct|Verity only|\"Xiaomi MiMo\" category in Verity's config menu\n\nFeatures\n- Chinese & English TTS with natural-language emotion/style control\n- Chinese speech recognition (ASR) \u2014 no more English-only local STT\n- Voice clone mode: clone Verity's in-game voice from the bundled intro sample (mimo-v2.5-tts-voiceclone) \u2014 or use preset voices like \u82cf\u6253 (Soda, Chinese male) / \u767d\u6866 (Baihua), \u51b0\u7cd6 (Bingtang) / \u8309\u8389 (Moliy), Mia / Chloe / Milo / Dean\n- Pay-as-you-go (sk- keys) or Token Plan (tp- keys) + cluster selection (China / Singapore / Europe)\n- Custom base URL override\n\nRequirements\n- Minecraft 1.20.1, Forge 47.x\n- Verity JE (\u2026) (6.0.0-beta.5+)\n- addon version: Smiley's Better Voice (\u2026) + Cloth Config\n- direct version: YACL (bundled as Verity dependency)\n- A MiMo API key: https://platform.xiaomimimo.com/#/console/api-keys\n\nQuick start (direct)\n1. Drop the jar into mods\n2. Open Verity's config \u2192 Xiaomi MiMo category\n3. Paste your MiMo API key, choose Plan (pay-as-you-go / Token Plan) and Cluster, enable MiMo TTS / MiMo ASR, pick a voice mode & voice (default \u82cf\u6253), set ASR language to zh\n4. Save and talk to Verity \u2014 in Chinese or English :)\n", "body_url": null, "published": "2026-08-17T20:12:34.616577Z", "updated": "2026-09-10T12:12:04.284268Z", "approved": "2026-09-24T19:47:27.365431Z", "queued": "2026-08-17T20:37:59.033608Z", "status": "approved", "requested_status": "approved", "moderator_message": null, "license": {"id": "MIT", "name": "MIT License", "url": null}, "downloads": 8, "followers": 0, "categories": ["optimization"], "additional_categories": [], "loaders": ["forge"], "versions": ["gOKKHsmA", "SqfwtCTQ", "Qkuv1Fu7", "4ma9v3St", "kNJ58f5J", "tRiJO1qp", "tT0yU50d", "c1IMOwmh", "58cfmzo1", "Hw8mzjbA", "BW3VSScN", "zFjd6VVM"], "icon_url": "https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/mEFIrXVS/3ad331b5d453eb4402d7fd45610898ef4fc8e4ed_96.webp", "raw_icon_url": "https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/mEFIrXVS/3ad331b5d453eb4402d7fd45610898ef4fc8e4ed.png", "issues_url": null, "source_url": "https://github.com/Enderman112/verity-mimo/tree/main", "wiki_url": null, "discord_url": null, "donation_urls": [], "gallery": [], "color": 16380244, "thread_id": "Z8M9vPZL", "monetization_status": "monetized"}, {"client_side": "unsupported", "server_side": "required", "game_versions": ["1.21.1"], "environment": ["server_only"], "id": "dLlwJXf6", "slug": "pvb", "project_type": "mod", "team": "C7uFy02R", "organization": null, "title": "PvB", "description": "Bots of different difficulties to fight with different kits and an arena world type", "body": "A Minecraft 1.21.1 Fabric mod that gives you a PvP opponent worth practising against.\n\nThe problem it solves is that you can't get better at Minecraft PvP alone. Command-block dummies don't fight back, mobs don't play like people, and finding a human who'll duel you fifty times in a row to drill one matchup is hard.\n\nThe bot is a real player. Not a mob wearing armour \u2014 an actual ServerPlayerEntity driven by an AI. That distinction matters more than it sounds: it means the bot inherits the genuine 1.9 attack cooldown, real sprint-reset knockback, shields with the correct 5-tick raise delay, authentic crystal placement rules and explosion falloff, totem pops, mace fall-damage scaling. Nothing is approximated. If you beat it, you beat the actual mechanics.\n\nIt's built to feel human, not perfect. Every reaction is a sampled delay, never a constant. The crosshair carries a slow drifting bias plus per-tick jitter, so it wanders like a hand on a mouse instead of snapping. There's a \"focus\" value that drifts across a fight, producing the they had a bad ten seconds effect. Mistakes cluster rather than firing independently \u2014 one error opens a short window where more are likely, which is what tilting actually looks like. Item switches cost real time and can grab the wrong hotbar slot under pressure. Each bot also rolls permanent quirks at spawn, so two Master bots don't play identically.\n\nDifficulty changes skill, never the toolset. An Easy bot owns crystals, a mace and pearls exactly like a Master bot \u2014 it's simply bad at using them. It aims 26\u00b0 off, reacts in a full second, forgets its totem, and pops crystals so slowly you walk out of the blast. Master reacts in ~1 tick and tracks you at 68\u00b0/second. Nine attributes drive all of it, and they're editable in a config file.\n\nRounds are built for repetition. Build an arena, pick a difficulty and kit, hit Fight. Whoever would die doesn't \u2014 the lethal hit is cancelled, so nothing drops, there's no death screen, the arena rebuilds itself, and a rematch screen appears a second later. You can run twenty rounds back-to-back without ever picking up loot or walking anywhere.\n\nThere are eleven kits \u2014 Crystal PvP, sword-only, potion, mace, UHC, Sumo and more \u2014 and they're independent of difficulty, so \"Master skill, sword-only kit\" is a thing you can pick. Restriction is real: a bot with no crystals genuinely never uses them, because the AI reads the inventory rather than a difficulty label.\n\nIt's server-side, so a whole server of vanilla clients can fight it with nothing installed.", "body_url": null, "published": "2026-08-06T08:29:38.944345Z", "updated": "2026-08-07T08:18:10.456497Z", "approved": "2026-09-24T19:50:37.891592Z", "queued": "2026-08-19T05:03:37.110821Z", "status": "approved", "requested_status": "approved", "moderator_message": null, "license": {"id": "LicenseRef-All-Rights-Reserved", "name": "", "url": null}, "downloads": 8, "followers": 0, "categories": [], "additional_categories": [], "loaders": ["fabric"], "versions": ["DYKJdF9b"], "icon_url": null, "raw_icon_url": null, "issues_url": null, "source_url": null, "wiki_url": null, "discord_url": null, "donation_urls": [], "gallery": [{"url": "https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/dLlwJXf6/images/a27c390d42057e8c63f4c9628503947065b40d87_350.webp", "raw_url": "https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/dLlwJXf6/images/a27c390d42057e8c63f4c9628503947065b40d87.png", "featured": false, "title": "Have fun!", "description": "Practice and play!", "created": "2026-08-06T08:35:11.356094Z", "ordering": 0}, {"url": "https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/dLlwJXf6/images/e2c19e30370f7337863d320019c8d62a6a6d987e_350.webp", "raw_url": "https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/dLlwJXf6/images/e2c19e30370f7337863d320019c8d62a6a6d987e.png", "featured": false, "title": "kit selection", "description": null, "created": "2026-08-06T08:34:25.153465Z", "ordering": 0}], "color": null, "thread_id": "b5L60eU0", "monetization_status": "monetized"}, {"client_side": "required", "server_side": "unsupported", "game_versions": ["1.21.11"], "environment": ["client_only"], "id": "J57VczQ5", "slug": "glitch-visuals", "project_type": "mod", "team": "eBgt0A7l", "organization": null, "title": "Glitch Visuals", "description": "These are simple visuals featuring only the most useful functions.", "body": "## Main Mod Features\n### 1. Shaders\nWorks only in conjunction with Iris Shaders. Quickly enable your disable shaders.\n### 2. Gamma\nTired of caves being too dark but can't be bothered to dig through game settings? Gamma lets you instantly brighten things up so night looks like day!\n### 3. Kill Effects\n![Laser striking the ground from the sky at the spot where a cow was killed](https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/cached_images/6822f2f7951fa1e5ed04b84715ae37fc02076ec7.png)\n\nBored of defeating mobs or players? Kill effects will spice things up!\n### 4. Better Near\nPlaying on a server and want to know who's nearby, but lack the necessary rank or find it too expensive? This feature lets you instantly see which players are within a 200-block radius.\n### 5. Markers\n![Green, blue, and red markers indicating trap locations](https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/cached_images/b854e260aa50a41b0917d45aa486b55a06915594_0.webp)\n\nNew to Minecraft and constantly forgetting where your base is? Or are you a trapper who can't remember where you placed that pressure plate? With markers, you'll never lose track of anything again!\n### 6. Configs\nLove having multiple setting presets but hate the hassle of switching between them? Configs let you create various presets and switch between them instantly.\n### 7. Inventory Animations\nFind it boring when crafting tables, furnaces, or chat messages just pop up instantly? This feature makes things more fun!\n### 8. Favorites\n![Hitboxes feature with a white favorites flag](https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/cached_images/5e0c4a7999265e29fb042cd0b0bb15bc96b58f62.png)\n\nDo you have specific settings you want quick access to? The Favorites section will open automatically whenever you launch the Glitch Visuals menu!\n\n## Sound Guide\n#### Our visuals support custom sounds. Here\u2019s how to set them up:\n1. Choose your sound\n2. Convert it to .ogg format using an online converter\n3. Move your sound file to `.minecraft/config/glitchvisuals/sounds`\n4. Select your sound in the \"Player\" section", "body_url": null, "published": "2026-08-11T15:37:22.790315Z", "updated": "2026-08-11T16:06:57.429774Z", "approved": "2026-09-24T18:49:35.131334Z", "queued": "2026-08-17T14:33:36.342550Z", "status": "approved", "requested_status": "approved", "moderator_message": null, "license": {"id": "LicenseRef-All-Rights-Reserved", "name": "", "url": null}, "downloads": 5, "followers": 0, "categories": ["decoration", "game-mechanics", "utility"], "additional_categories": ["management"], "loaders": ["fabric"], "versions": ["n3DiWFTG"], "icon_url": "https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/J57VczQ5/0bd6cebac5114b46c2e586601d07d26a2dc3d35c_96.webp", "raw_icon_url": "https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/J57VczQ5/0bd6cebac5114b46c2e586601d07d26a2dc3d35c.jpeg", "issues_url": null, "source_url": null, "wiki_url": null, "discord_url": null, "donation_urls": [], "gallery": [{"url": "https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/J57VczQ5/images/581eca4788e93a06e01988b37ed1cfb797081e3a_350.webp", "raw_url": "https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/J57VczQ5/images/581eca4788e93a06e01988b37ed1cfb797081e3a.png", "featured": false, "title": "Armor UI", "description": "\u041d\u0430 \u044d\u0442\u043e\u043c \u0438\u0437\u043e\u0431\u0440\u0430\u0436\u0435\u043d\u0438\u0438 \u0432\u0438\u0434\u043d\u043e \u043f\u0440\u0438\u043c\u0435\u043d\u0435\u043d\u0438\u0435 \u0444\u0443\u043d\u043a\u0446\u0438\u0438 Armor UI", "created": "2026-08-12T05:51:07.993898Z", "ordering": 0}, {"url": "https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/J57VczQ5/images/eb0540b341b7f977c547cc3337b641b007c64c66_350.webp", "raw_url": "https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/J57VczQ5/images/eb0540b341b7f977c547cc3337b641b007c64c66.png", "featured": false, "title": "\u041c\u0435\u0442\u043a\u0438", "description": "\u041d\u0430\u0433\u043b\u044f\u0434\u043d\u043e\u0435  \u0438\u0441\u043f\u043e\u043b\u044c\u0437\u043e\u0432\u0430\u043d\u0438\u0435 \u0444\u0443\u043d\u043a\u0446\u0438\u0438 \"\u041c\u0435\u0442\u043a\u0438\"", "created": "2026-08-12T05:46:35.416832Z", "ordering": 0}, {"url": "https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/J57VczQ5/images/ee592790afed7ed9c47726969f9893739eed4400_350.webp", "raw_url": "https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/J57VczQ5/images/ee592790afed7ed9c47726969f9893739eed4400.png", "featured": false, "title": "\u0413\u043b\u0430\u0432\u043d\u043e\u0435 \u043c\u0435\u043d\u044e", "description": "\u041c\u043e\u0436\u043d\u043e \u0443\u0432\u0438\u0434\u0435\u0442\u044c \u0433\u043b\u0430\u0432\u043d\u044b\u0435 \u043a\u043b\u0438\u0435\u043d\u0442\u0441\u043a\u0438\u0435 \u0444\u0443\u043d\u043a\u0446\u0438\u0438", "created": "2026-08-12T05:49:01.240162Z", "ordering": 0}], "color": 525323, "thread_id": "ZheUCvQL", "monetization_status": "monetized"}, {"client_side": "unknown", "server_side": "unknown", "game_versions": ["1.12", "1.12.1", "1.12.2", "1.13", "1.13.1", "1.13.2", "1.14", "1.14.1", "1.14.2", "1.14.3", "1.14.4", "1.15", "1.15.1", "1.15.2", "1.16", "1.16.1", "1.16.2", "1.16.3", "1.16.4", "1.16.5", "1.17", "1.17.1", "1.18", "1.18.1", "1.18.2", "1.19", "1.19.1", "1.19.2", "1.19.3", "1.19.4", "1.20", "1.20.1", "1.20.2", "1.20.3", "1.20.4", "1.20.5", "1.20.6", "1.21", "1.21.1", "1.21.2", "1.21.3", "1.21.4", "1.21.5", "1.21.6", "1.21.7", "1.21.8", "1.21.9", "1.21.10", "1.21.11", "26.1", "26.1.1", "26.1.2", "26.2"], "environment": ["client_and_server"], "id": "zTyCkKJj", "slug": "openqqauth", "project_type": "mod", "team": "quqKCzp3", "organization": null, "title": "OpenQQAuth", "description": "QQ-driven login & account authentication for Minecraft (Velocity): offline, premium, Bedrock and token login.", "body": "# OpenQQAuth\n\n**QQ-driven login & account authentication system for Minecraft** \u2014 an open-source MQE alternative and beyond.\n\nOpenQQAuth runs on the **Velocity proxy**: players are isolated behind a graphical authentication gate (dialog screens, virtual chest menu, virtual anvil \u2014 adapted across every protocol generation) until their identity is verified, then released to the backend Paper server. It uses **QQ as the mandatory ownership credential for every account** and supports three login methods:\n\n- **Offline password login** \u2014 enter your password in the virtual anvil\n- **Premium fast login** \u2014 encrypted handshake + hasJoined verification, passwordless once bound to QQ\n- **Bedrock login** \u2014 Microsoft account identity (Floodgate), passwordless after QQ binding, with optional inheritance of a Java account's data\n\nIt also adds a **login token** system: after installing the Fabric / NeoForge dual-platform mod, players can click **\"Connect with Token\"** in the multiplayer screen and enter a credential privately sent by the QQ group bot for instant passwordless entry (30-day validity, revocable).\n\n> Domain glossary: [`CONTEXT.md`](CONTEXT.md) \u00b7 Architecture decisions: [`docs/adr/`](docs/adr/) \u00b7 Spec: [`.scratch/qqauth/spec.md`](.scratch/qqauth/spec.md) \u00b7 External API research: [`.scratch/qqauth/api-reference.md`](.scratch/qqauth/api-reference.md)\n\n## Table of Contents\n\n- [Features](#features)\n- [Architecture](#architecture)\n- [Requirements](#requirements)\n- [Quick Start](#quick-start)\n- [Configuration Reference](#configuration-reference)\n- [QQ Group Commands](#qq-group-commands)\n- [In-Game Commands](#in-game-commands)\n- [Login & Binding Flows](#login--binding-flows)\n- [Login Tokens (mod)](#login-tokens-mod)\n- [Chat Sync](#chat-sync)\n- [Permission Model](#permission-model)\n- [Building from Source](#building-from-source)\n- [Supported Versions](#supported-versions)\n- [Development Guide](#development-guide)\n- [FAQ](#faq)\n- [License](#license)\n\n## Features\n\n- **Gate**: unverified connections are confined to the login screen until authenticated, then released to the backend server\n- **Graphical authentication UI**: dialog screens (1.21.6+) and virtual chest menus (older versions) for login-method selection; password entry always uses a virtual anvil (open / rename / left-click confirm / right-click clear / gray concrete to reset)\n- **Full protocol-generation support**: anvil packets and item serialization are parameterized per protocol family (Legacy 1.7.2~1.12.2 / Flat 1.13~1.14.4 / Classic NBT 1.15~1.20.4 / Components 1.20.5~1.21.1 / Menu Refactor 1.21.2~1.21.5 / Dialog 1.21.6+), with rename-transport split (\u22641.12.2 plugin channel / 1.13+ rename packet)\n- **Three login methods**: offline password, premium fast login (encrypted handshake + hasJoined double check), and passwordless Bedrock\n- **QQ binding**: verification-code flow (in-game code \u2192 send `bind <code>` in the group; sender QQ must match the target QQ, preventing code sniping)\n- **Premium binding**: clickable chat hint to trigger, premium session + QQ verification code as two factors; `premiumUuid`-based matching survives name changes; `/opa bindpremium` for cross-name binding; impersonation protection (reject offline logins on premium-bound names + anti-sockpuppet account creation)\n- **Bedrock support**: Floodgate detection, Cumulus form binding, `/opa bindxbox` inheritance binding (share a Java account's location/inventory), Java/Bedrock mutual exclusivity, `/opa unbindxbox` to restore an independent identity\n- **Fast login**: same-IP reconnect within 30 minutes after \u226510 minutes online is passwordless (once per window); QQ notification on trigger (\"not you? reply freeze\", toggleable)\n- **Login tokens**: `\u83b7\u53d6\u51ed\u8bc1` in the group \u2192 bot sends a credential privately \u2192 mod-side \"Connect with Token\"; 30-day validity, revocable; replay-protected (one-time nonce challenge-response)\n- **Remote self-service & administration from QQ**: `kick` / `freeze` / `unfreeze` / `ban` / `unban` / `list` / `status` / `check` / `exec` / `reload` / `reconnect`\n- **Voluntary transfer**: on name conflict, the original owner unbinds \u2192 admin confirms via `transfer confirm` \u2192 target takes over (ADR-0007, no forced takeover path)\n- **Domain events**: `PlayerAuthenticatedEvent` / `AccountBoundEvent` / `AccountFrozenEvent` / `AccountBannedEvent` published for other plugins via Bukkit ServicesManager\n- **Read-only API**: `ReadOnlyAuthApi` for Paper-side plugins (economy / land claims / whitelist integrations)\n- **Chat sync**: optional bidirectional group \u2194 in-game chat forwarding\n- **i18n**: bilingual messages (zh_CN / en_US) with full translation-key coverage\n- **Security**: password hashing (jBCrypt), failed-attempt lockout (5 tries / 1 min), per-IP session limits, bind rate limiting, session timeouts, replay protection, audit log for all admin operations\n\n## Architecture\n\n```\n\u250c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2510     \u250c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2510     \u250c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2510\n\u2502  Minecraft   \u2502\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u25b6\u2502  Velocity (OpenQQAuth gate)  \u2502\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u25b6\u2502  Paper server \u2502\n\u2502  client      \u2502     \u2502  dialog/chest/anvil auth UI   \u2502     \u2502 (API/events) \u2502\n\u2514\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2518     \u2502  LoginPipeline decision core  \u2502     \u2514\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2518\n                     \u2502  handshake/premium/Bedrock    \u2502\n                     \u2514\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u252c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2518\n                                    \u2502 OneBot (WebSocket)\n                     \u250c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u25bc\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2510\n                     \u2502   QQ group bot (bind/admin)  \u2502\n                     \u2514\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2518\n```\n\n| Module | Description |\n|---|---|\n| `core` | All domain logic: accounts / verify codes / state machines / login pipeline / tokens / event bus / command framework, platform-independent |\n| `bootstrap/velocity` | Velocity proxy plugin: gate, virtual window UI, protocol-family codecs, OneBot wiring, mod login queries |\n| `bootstrap/paper` | Paper plugin: read-only API exposure (Bukkit ServicesManager), domain-event subscription example |\n| `bootstrap/bukkit` / `bungeecord` | Template compatibility skeletons (load-placeholder only) |\n| `bootstrap/fabric` + `bootstrap/neoforge` | Dual-platform jar: client-side \"Connect with Token\" UI & token transport, server-side placeholder |\n| `build-logic` | Gradle convention plugins (unified Java/Kotlin compile, checkstyle, spotless) |\n\n## Requirements\n\n- **Java 21** (build & run)\n- **Gradle 9.6.1** (system-installed; this project does not use the Gradle wrapper)\n- **Velocity proxy** (the production login-gate host)\n- **An OneBot 11 implementation** (e.g. [NapCat](https://github.com/NapNeko/NapCatQQ) / [go-cqhttp](https://github.com/Mrs4s/go-cqhttp)) over WebSocket\n- **Paper server** (backend)\n- Optional: **Floodgate / Geyser** (Bedrock support), **Fabric / NeoForge client mod** (token login)\n\n## Quick Start\n\n### 1. Build\n\n```bash\ngradle --no-daemon :bootstrap:velocity:build   # Velocity plugin\ngradle --no-daemon :bootstrap:paper:build      # Paper plugin\ngradle --no-daemon :bootstrap:fabric:build :bootstrap:neoforge:build  # mod dual-platform jar\n```\n\nArtifacts land in each module's `build/libs/`.\n\n### 2. Install\n\n1. Put the velocity plugin jar in `velocity/plugins/`, the paper jar in `paper/plugins/`\n2. Start Velocity once to generate the default `config.yml`, then edit as needed (see [Configuration Reference](#configuration-reference))\n3. Configure the QQ bot (OneBot 11 WebSocket): set `qq-bot.ws-url` and `qq-bot.ws-token`, and add admin QQs to `qq-bot.admin-qqs`\n4. Restart Velocity; send `reload` in the group or run `/opa reload` as an admin to hot-reload config\n\n### 3. Minimal working configuration\n\n```yaml\nconfig-version: 1\nqq-bot:\n  ws-url: \"ws://127.0.0.1:6700\"   # OneBot WebSocket endpoint\n  ws-token: \"\"                    # access token (if auth enabled)\n  admin-qqs:                      # admin QQ list\n    - \"10001\"\nlogin:\n  max-failed-attempts: 5          # password lockout threshold\n  lockout-minutes: 1              # lockout duration (minutes)\nstorage:\n  driver: sqlite\n  sqlite-file: openqqauth.db\n```\n\n## Configuration Reference\n\nAll configuration lives in `config.yml` in the Velocity plugin directory (`QqAuthConfiguration`, loaded via Configurate).\n\n### `qq-bot` (OneBot)\n\n| Key | Default | Description |\n|---|---|---|\n| `qq-bot.ws-url` | `ws://127.0.0.1:6700` | OneBot 11 WebSocket endpoint |\n| `qq-bot.ws-token` | `\"\"` | Access token |\n| `qq-bot.admin-qqs` | `[]` | Admin QQ list (ADMIN permission) |\n\n### `accounts`\n\n| Key | Default | Description |\n|---|---|---|\n| `accounts.per-qq-limit` | `3` | Max accounts bindable to a single QQ |\n\n### `login`\n\n| Key | Default | Description |\n|---|---|---|\n| `login.fast-login-window` | `30` | Fast-login window (minutes): passwordless reconnect time span |\n| `login.fast-login-min-online-minutes` | `10` | Prior online time required to trigger fast login (minutes) |\n| `login.fast-login-notify-qq` | `true` | Notify the bound QQ when fast login triggers |\n| `login.max-failed-attempts` | `5` | Password lockout threshold |\n| `login.lockout-minutes` | `1` | Lockout duration (minutes) |\n| `login.max-sessions-per-ip` | `3` | Max concurrent sessions per IP (excess rejected) |\n| `login.bind-frequency-per-minute` | `3` | Bind rate limit (per minute) |\n| `login.session-timeout-seconds` | `300` | Session timeout kick (seconds) |\n| `login.bind-timeout-seconds` | `180` | Binding flow timeout (seconds) |\n| `login.inherit-bind-window-minutes` | `5` | Bedrock inheritance-binding window (minutes) |\n| `login.max-name-length` | `30` | Max rename input length |\n\n### `verify-code`\n\n| Key | Default | Description |\n|---|---|---|\n| `verify-code.length` | `4` | Verification code length |\n| `verify-code.expire-seconds` | `180` | Verification code validity (seconds) |\n\n### `token`\n\n| Key | Default | Description |\n|---|---|---|\n| `token.enabled` | `true` | Enable the token login path |\n| `token.ttl-days` | `30` | Token validity (days) |\n\n### `sync-groups` (chat sync)\n\n| Key | Default | Description |\n|---|---|---|\n| `sync-groups.enabled` | `false` | Enable message sync |\n| `sync-groups.group-ids` | `[]` | Group IDs participating in sync |\n| `sync-groups.game-to-group` | `true` | In-game \u2192 group forwarding |\n| `sync-groups.group-to-game` | `true` | Group \u2192 in-game forwarding |\n| `sync-groups.merge-window-seconds` | `5` | Merge window (seconds) |\n| `sync-groups.max-forwards-per-minute` | `10` | Max forwards per minute |\n\n### `storage`\n\n| Key | Default | Description |\n|---|---|---|\n| `storage.driver` | `sqlite` | Storage driver (SQLite currently) |\n| `storage.sqlite-file` | `openqqauth.db` | SQLite database file path |\n\n### `premium` (premium detection)\n\n| Key | Default | Description |\n|---|---|---|\n| `premium.enabled` | `true` | Enable premium detection |\n| `premium.name-query-cache-hours` | `24` | Name\u2192UUID query cache duration (hours) |\n| `premium.http-timeout-seconds` | `5` | Mojang API timeout (seconds) |\n| `premium.rate-limit-per-window` | `600` | Max queries per rate-limit window |\n| `premium.rate-limit-window-minutes` | `10` | Rate-limit window (minutes) |\n| `premium.bind-wait-minutes` | `5` | Premium binding wait-marker duration (minutes) |\n\n## QQ Group Commands\n\n> Commands are received by the QQ group bot. Permission tiers: see [Permission Model](#permission-model).\n\n### Player self-service (`BOUND_MEMBER`)\n\n| Command | Description |\n|---|---|\n| `kick` | Kick all online accounts of the sender (self-service against abnormal logins) |\n| `freeze` | Freeze the sender's accounts (temporary, self-reversible) |\n| `unfreeze` | Unfreeze the sender's accounts |\n| `status` | Show the sender's account info & verification state |\n| `list` | Show the online list |\n| `\u83b7\u53d6\u51ed\u8bc1` | Issue a new login token for the sender's account and send it privately (re-issuing overrides the old one) |\n| `\u540a\u9500\u51ed\u8bc1 [<account>]` | Immediately revoke the tokens of the sender's accounts |\n\n### Verification-code commands (in-group confirmation)\n\n| Command | Description |\n|---|---|\n| `bind <code>` | Confirm QQ binding (code shown on the in-game screen) |\n| `\u91cd\u7f6e <code>` | Confirm password reset (started from the gray concrete in the anvil) |\n| `\u89e3\u7ed1\u6b63\u7248 <code>` | Unbind the premium identity |\n| `\u89e3\u7ed1\u57fa\u5ca9 <code>` | Unbind the Bedrock account (restore independent identity) |\n\n### Admin commands (`ADMIN`)\n\n| Command | Description |\n|---|---|\n| `bind 1 <QQ> <player>` | Force-bind an account (a token is then sent privately) |\n| `bind 2 <QQ>` | Reset an account's password (new password printed to console) |\n| `ban @<target> [name]` / `unban` | Ban / unban an account (persistent, admin-only) |\n| `freeze @<target> [name]` / `unfreeze` | Freeze / unfreeze any account (temporary, reversible) |\n| `check` | View any player's full info & server overview |\n| `exec <server> <command>` | Run a command on the backend server (audit-logged before/after) |\n| `transfer confirm <account> <targetQQ> <premiumName>` | Confirm a voluntary transfer (after the owner unbinds) |\n| `transfer list` | List pending transfer confirmations |\n| `reload` | Hot-reload configuration |\n| `reconnect` | Reconnect the QQ bot |\n\n## In-Game Commands\n\nIn-game commands use the `/opa` prefix (Velocity command registration):\n\n| Command | Description |\n|---|---|\n| `/opa bindpremium <name>` | Cross-name premium binding (premium identity takes over the original offline account) |\n| `/opa bindxbox <name>` | Start Bedrock inheritance binding (Bedrock account \u2192 specified Java account, sharing location/inventory) |\n| `/opa unbindxbox` | Unbind Bedrock inheritance (restore independent identity, data kept) |\n| `/opa reload` | Hot-reload configuration (admin) |\n\n## Login & Binding Flows\n\n### New player (offline)\n\n1. Join the server \u2192 intercepted by the gate, enters the QQ binding flow directly\n2. Enter your QQ number \u2192 the in-game screen shows a verification code\n3. Send `bind <code>` in the QQ group (sender QQ must match the entered QQ \u2014 anti-sniping)\n4. Binding succeeds \u2192 create a password in the anvil (two confirmation inputs) \u2192 released into the server\n\n### Returning player (offline)\n\n- Select \"offline\" on the login screen \u2192 enter your password in the anvil \u2192 verified and released\n- Forgot your password: click the gray concrete in the anvil to start a reset \u2192 set a new password \u2192 confirm with `\u91cd\u7f6e <code>` in the group\n\n### Premium player\n\n1. When the name matches a premium account, the chat shows \"detected [id] has a premium account \u2014 bind?\"\n2. Click the hint \u2192 kicked with \"use a premium client to join\"\n3. Reconnect with the premium client \u2192 encrypted handshake + hasJoined verification \u2192 send `\u7ed1\u5b9a\u6b63\u7248 <code>` in the group to complete the QQ second factor\n4. After binding, premium logins are passwordless (account matched by `premiumUuid` with identity rewrite; name changes don't matter)\n5. Same person with a different name: `/opa bindpremium` for manual cross-name binding\n\n### Bedrock player (Floodgate)\n\n1. Floodgate detects the Bedrock connection \u2192 skips the Java login screens, uses a Cumulus form to enter the QQ number directly\n2. Send `bind <code>` in the group to confirm \u2192 bound and released (passwordless)\n3. `/opa bindxbox`: inheritance-bind the Bedrock account to a Java account (shared location/inventory), Java/Bedrock mutually exclusive online\n4. `/opa unbindxbox` or `\u89e3\u7ed1\u57fa\u5ca9` in the group: restore an independent identity (data kept while under the QQ account limit)\n\n### Fast login\n\n- On reconnect: same IP within 30 minutes, previously online \u226510 minutes \u2192 passwordless auto-release (once per window)\n- QQ notification on trigger: \"account <name> just joined via fast login \u2014 not you? reply freeze\" (toggleable via `fast-login-notify-qq`)\n\n## Login Tokens (mod)\n\n### For players\n\n1. Send `\u83b7\u53d6\u51ed\u8bc1` in the QQ group \u2192 the bot privately sends a 30-day token\n2. Launch a client with the OpenQQAuth mod installed (Fabric or NeoForge)\n3. Click **\"Connect with Token\"** in the bottom-right of the multiplayer screen \u2192 enter the token \u2192 connect\n4. The server verifies and releases you passwordless; revoke at any time with `\u540a\u9500\u51ed\u8bc1` if the token leaks\n\n### How it works\n\n- During the login phase the token is sent over the mod channel (`openqqauth:token`); the Velocity side runs a 128-bit random nonce challenge-response to prevent replay\n- Verification (`TokenLoginChecker`): token + account binding + not expired + not revoked \u2192 passwordless release on hit\n- A failed token check never blocks the password path (the player stays at the password screen)\n- Non-mod (vanilla) clients are unaffected and use password login as usual\n- Optional local plaintext token storage (`save-token` toggle; cleared when disabled)\n\n## Chat Sync\n\nWith `sync-groups.enabled`:\n\n- Group messages \u2192 in-game chat (`group-to-game`)\n- In-game chat \u2192 group (`game-to-group`)\n- In-game `/opa at` to @ a group member, `/opa re` to reply to a group message\n\n## Permission Model\n\n| Tier | Meaning | How to get |\n|---|---|---|\n| `ANY` | Any group member | Default |\n| `BOUND_MEMBER` | Player with a bound account | Complete QQ binding |\n| `ADMIN` | Administrator | Set `qq-bot.admin-qqs` |\n\nAdmin commands (`bind` / `ban` / `exec` / `check` / `transfer` / `reload` / `reconnect`, etc.) are written to the `CommandAuditLog` before and after execution.\n\n## Building from Source\n\n```bash\n# Full build: compile + test + checkstyle + spotless\ngradle --no-daemon build\n\n# Compile a single module\ngradle --no-daemon :core:compileJava\ngradle --no-daemon :bootstrap:velocity:compileJava\ngradle --no-daemon :bootstrap:paper:compileJava\ngradle --no-daemon :bootstrap:fabric:compileJava\ngradle --no-daemon :bootstrap:neoforge:compileJava\n\n# Run a module's tests\ngradle --no-daemon :core:test\ngradle --no-daemon :bootstrap:velocity:test\n\n# Style checks\ngradle --no-daemon :core:checkstyleMain :core:spotlessCheck\n```\n\n> System-installed Gradle 9.6.1 is required (no wrapper). Build memory of `-Xmx2G` is recommended (see `gradle.properties`).\n\n## Supported Versions\n\n### Client Minecraft versions (protocol families)\n\n| Protocol family | MC versions | Protocol | Support |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Legacy | 1.7.2 ~ 1.12.2 | 4 ~ 340 | \u2705 **1.12.2 committed**; 1.7.2~1.12.1 theoretical floor, not committed (packet-ID drift) |\n| Flat | 1.13 ~ 1.14.4 | 393 ~ 498 | \u26a0\ufe0f calibrated on 1.14.4; earlier 1.13 sub-versions not committed |\n| Classic NBT | 1.15 ~ 1.20.4 | 573 ~ 765 | \u2705 |\n| Components | 1.20.5 ~ 1.21.1 | 766 ~ 767 | \u2705 |\n| Menu Refactor | 1.21.2 ~ 1.21.5 | 768 ~ 770 | \u2705 |\n| Dialog | 1.21.6 ~ latest (26.2) | 771+ | \u2705 |\n\n**Conclusion: clients from 1.12.2 up to the latest release (26.2) can log in.** The UI auto-dispatches per version: dialog screens for 1.21.6+, virtual chest menus for older versions, and a virtual anvil for password input everywhere (rename split: \u22641.12.2 plugin channel / 1.13+ rename packet; item serialization: NBT \u22641.20.4 / Data Components \u22651.20.5).\n\n### Runtime requirements\n\n| Side | Version |\n|---|---|\n| **Velocity proxy** | Velocity API 3.5.0-SNAPSHOT (Velocity 3.3.x series), Java 21 |\n| **Java** | 21 |\n| **Paper server** | any version proxied by that Velocity release |\n| **Gradle** | 9.6.1 (build only) |\n| **mod side (token login)** | Fabric (fabric-loom 1.17.9) / NeoForge (ModDevGradle 2.0.141), target MC **26.1.2** (build baseline) |\n\n### Known limits\n\n1. **1.7.2~1.12.1**: the Legacy constant table exists, but this range is marked \"theoretical floor, not committed\" \u2014 packet-ID drift may occur; **1.12.2 is the recommended minimum for production**\n2. **mod token side**: the build baseline is MC 26.1.2; supporting other MC versions requires bumping `minecraft = \"26.1.2\"` in the build config and rebuilding\n3. **real Velocity connection wiring**: ServerboundPacketHandler bridging for old families (<770) is a follow-up ticket; verified at the mock layer\n\n## Development Guide\n\n- **Issues & spec**: `.scratch/<feature>/` (spec + numbered tickets), see `docs/agents/issue-tracker.md`\n- **Triage labels**: `needs-triage` / `needs-info` / `ready-for-agent` / `ready-for-human` / `wontfix`, see `docs/agents/triage-labels.md`\n- **Domain glossary**: `CONTEXT.md` (account / QQ / bind / gate / login screen / premium binding / inheritance binding, etc.)\n- **Architecture decisions**: `docs/adr/0001~0008` (virtual-anvil gate, offline premium detection, OneBot 11, login-screen layering, login tokens, fixed account keys, name conflict, fast-login trust model)\n- **Collaboration conventions**: see `CLAUDE.md` (worktree isolation, impact-scope verification, per-ticket commits, concurrency cap)\n\n### Core source layout\n\n```\ncore/src/main/java/dev/nmouzh/openqqauth/\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 account/      # account model, SQLite repository\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 anvil/        # anvil window state machine (UI-agnostic core)\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 api/          # read-only query API (for Paper plugins)\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 bedrock/      # Bedrock support (form sender, bind flow)\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 configuration/# config model (Configurate)\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 event/        # domain event bus (SimpleDomainEventBus)\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 gate/         # LoginPipeline, sessions, lockout, fast login\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 i18n/         # TranslationKey enum + bilingual resources\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 mojang/       # Mojang API client (name\u2192UUID, hasJoined)\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 onebot/       # OneBot 11 client (WebSocket messaging)\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 password/     # password hashing (jBCrypt)\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 qq/           # QQ domain: bind/reset/unbind state machines, group commands, audit log, voluntary transfer\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 token/        # login tokens: issue/revoke/verify, transport protocol, mod channel\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 util/         # utilities\n\u2514\u2500\u2500 verify/       # verification code service\n```\n\n## FAQ\n\n**Q: \"Bot offline\" \u2014 can't bind?**\nA: New-player binding checks the bot's online state (`BotOnlineProvider`); when the bot is offline, binding operations degrade to a hint + kick. Confirm the OneBot connection (`reconnect` reconnects).\n\n**Q: Old clients like 1.12.2 can't log in?**\nA: The anvil protocol and item serialization are parameterized per protocol family supporting the Legacy range (theoretical floor 1.7.2, 1.12.2 committed). Earlier 1.13 sub-versions and 1.7.2~1.12.1 packet-ID drift are \"not committed\"; real Velocity connection wiring (internal MinecraftConnection bridging) is a separate follow-up ticket.\n\n**Q: What happens if token verification fails?**\nA: It never blocks the password path \u2014 the failure is only logged and the player stays at the password screen and can log in normally.\n\n**Q: How can other plugins read account info?**\nA: On Paper, get `ReadOnlyAuthApi` (account/session queries) via Bukkit ServicesManager, and subscribe to domain events (`PlayerAuthenticatedEvent`, etc.). See `PaperAuthEvents` in `bootstrap/paper` for an integration example.\n\n**Q: Where is data stored?**\nA: By default in the SQLite file `openqqauth.db` (`storage.sqlite-file` is configurable).\n\n**Q: How are name conflicts handled?**\nA: Per ADR-0007 (\"first come, first served for the past; premium-priority for the future\"): conflicting parties can use voluntary transfer (owner unbinds \u2192 admin `transfer confirm` \u2192 target takes over). The system provides no forced-takeover path.\n\n## License\n\nThis project is licensed under [CC0 1.0 Universal](LICENSE) \u2014 free to use however you like, including relicensing for your own projects.\n", "body_url": null, "published": "2026-08-09T06:28:40.983169Z", "updated": "2026-08-14T14:43:45.218391Z", "approved": "2026-09-24T17:54:43.973170Z", "queued": "2026-08-14T14:59:53.615528Z", "status": "approved", "requested_status": "approved", "moderator_message": null, "license": {"id": "LicenseRef--CC0-1.0-Universal-", "name": "", "url": "https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/legalcode.en"}, "downloads": 6, "followers": 0, "categories": ["library", "management", "utility"], "additional_categories": [], "loaders": ["bukkit", "bungeecord", "fabric", "neoforge", "paper", "velocity"], "versions": ["NpUTizW0", "YfcP6Vu8", "mVgtVvI9", "DXugGDnc", "GHhzmKnz", "t1TEjryx"], "icon_url": "https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/zTyCkKJj/9c0daf0ec74eaeb2fd64078191721c6986e9159c_96.webp", "raw_icon_url": "https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/zTyCkKJj/9c0daf0ec74eaeb2fd64078191721c6986e9159c.png", "issues_url": null, "source_url": null, "wiki_url": null, "discord_url": null, "donation_urls": [], "gallery": [{"url": "https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/zTyCkKJj/images/53024aefc753eba58e72b83d9495eb2f047e4242_350.webp", "raw_url": "https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/zTyCkKJj/images/53024aefc753eba58e72b83d9495eb2f047e4242.png", "featured": false, "title": "logo", "description": null, "created": "2026-08-14T14:56:00.804722Z", "ordering": 0}], "color": 5414964, "thread_id": "WEOZcEfh", "monetization_status": "monetized"}, {"client_side": "required", "server_side": "required", "game_versions": ["1.21.1"], "environment": ["client_and_server"], "id": "roJlZcNx", "slug": "great-sage", "project_type": "mod", "team": "aEsCbx9D", "organization": null, "title": "Great Sage - Tensura Reincarnated Addon", "description": "Gives the Great Sage its voice. Every skill you unlock is announced out loud \u2014 by name \u2014 with a full anime-style cutscene. 227 voice lines covering all 212 skills.", "body": "# Great Sage\n\n**The Great Sage finally has a voice \u2014 and now it answers back.**\n\nAn addon for **Tensura: Reincarnated** that gives *Daikenja* what the base mod\nnever had time to give it: a voice, a presence, and something to say.\n\nEvery skill you unlock gets announced out loud, in Japanese, with clips from the\nshow. Every evolution. Every awakening. And since 0.0.4 it does more than react \u2014\nit has an interface you can open, it reads creatures for you, and it comments on\nwhat you are doing while you play.\n\n**759 voice clips \u00b7 546 skills \u00b7 140 species \u00b7 8 mods supported**\n\n---\n\n## Watch it in action\n\nPreviews and gameplay on my channel:\n\n### \u25b6 https://www.youtube.com/@astro2023\n\n---\n\n## Why this exists\n\nI kept unlocking skills in Tensura and reading them in chat. That was it. No\nvoice. The single most iconic thing about the Great Sage \u2014 that flat, calm system\nvoice telling you exactly what you just gained \u2014 was not there.\n\nWhat I found announced skill *tiers* with generic jingles. One sound for \"you got\na unique skill\". None of them say **the name of the skill**.\n\nSo I recorded them. All of them.\n\n---\n\n## It announces what you gain\n\nUnlock a skill and Great Sage says it. Not a chat line \u2014 the full thing.\n\nA wireframe icosahedron computed in real 3D, ringed by orbital bands, crossed by\ndashed rays. The skill name **slams into place** with an impact sound.\n\nThe core **breathes with the voice**: it swells on peaks, edges brighten, rays\nstretch. That is not a loop. Every clip's amplitude envelope is computed when the\nsounds are built and shipped with the mod, so the visuals follow the actual audio\nbeing spoken, syllable by syllable.\n\nUnlock ten skills at once and you get **one** announcement, grouped by class \u2014\nnot ten stacked on top of each other.\n\nPrefer something discreet? **Quiet mode** puts Great Sage in the bottom right\ncorner with a small bubble instead of taking the screen. Same voice, nothing\ndarkened, you keep playing.\n\n## It announces what you become\n\n**Species evolution** gets its own scene. Great Sage states the conditions are\nmet, addresses a petition to the Voice of the World, **waits** \u2014 deliberately\nlong, because nothing says it will be granted \u2014 then confirms, and names the\nspecies you are leaving and the one you are becoming.\n\nThe core charges until it cannot hold. The shell **bursts into twenty solid\nplates**, each tumbling with a trail. The naked core beats alone. Then a new\nshell, four times denser, **crystallises outward from the centre** and locks into\nplace on the exact frame the new species name lands.\n\nThe five progression steps each have their own presentation and their own\nrecorded line: **Hero Egg \u00b7 Demon Lord Seed \u00b7 Harvest Festival \u00b7 True Hero \u00b7\nTrue Demon Lord.** During the two awakenings you cannot take damage \u2014 the\nanimation is long and you cannot move.\n\n## It has a menu \u2014 press **G**\n\nOnly if you actually carry the Great Sage skill.\n\nThe shell does not fade in. Its thirty edges **fly in from outside the screen**,\nspinning and trailing, and lock into place with a flash. The faculties **orbit\naround the core**, tied to it by sagging threads. Closing plays it backwards.\n\n**Analyzing** \u2014 Great Sage decomposes a skill so you master it *without ever\nusing it*. The price is real and enforced server side: **the skill cannot be used\nwhile it is being analysed**. Duration scales with rarity, from twice as long for\na common up to eight times for an ultimate. Progress lives on the server, so\nclosing the menu or logging out changes nothing.\n\n**Records** \u2014 every skill in your modpack, not just the ones you have. Class,\nmastery percentage, magicule cost to learn, and which mod it came from. Useful\nwhen you have no idea which addon added the thing. Searchable.\n\n**Observations** \u2014 everything you have scanned, kept on file: the creature's **3D\nmodel**, its abilities grouped by class, and its **average existence value across\nevery reading**, with the sample count. Two goblins are not the same goblin, so\nkeeping the last number seen would be keeping an accident.\n\n## It reads the world \u2014 press **V**\n\nAssess mode. The interface disappears exactly like F1 and a blue filter drops\nover everything.\n\nEvery living thing gets an **aura sized by its existence value** \u2014 logarithmic,\nso a creature a thousand times stronger does not fill the screen. Auras are\nvisible **through walls**: an aura is a reading of power, not an object in the\nworld.\n\nLock a target, hold the key, stay within range, and the ring fills. You get its\nspecies, existence value, health and its rarest abilities \u2014 and the sheet lands\nin your Observations.\n\n**Standing near something far above you makes you sick.** Real nausea, and it\nscales with the gap.\n\nAnd **not everything can be read.** Past a certain threshold the target refuses.\nGreat Sage says so, the screen tears itself apart, the mode cuts out \u2014 and\nnothing about the target is revealed.\n\n## It talks to you\n\n**Thirty lines** it says on its own, based on what you are doing:\n\n- ore hidden behind the block you just broke\n- a cavity right under your feet\n- lava three blocks away\n- something walking up behind you\n- a tool about to break, or a better pickaxe sleeping in your bag\n- an abnormally magicule-dense area\n- your existence value approaching an evolution\n\nIt is deliberately restrained. There is a general silence between any two\ncomments, and the ones that stop being useful have a cap \u2014 \"it's dark here\" is\nworth saying six times, not sixty. Warnings that can save your life have no cap.\nAll of it is configurable, and one switch turns the whole thing off.\n\n---\n\n## Coverage\n\nEvery skill in the **ZS pack** is voiced, across eight mods:\n\n| Mod | Status |\n|---|---|\n| Tensura: Reincarnated | \u2714 base |\n| Tensura Mysticism | \u2714 |\n| Elite Tensura | \u2714 |\n| Tensura More Skills | \u2714 |\n| TR Origins | \u2714 |\n| TR Starlight | \u2714 |\n| TR Ascension | \u2714 |\n| TR Nightmare | \u2714 |\n\n**546 skill clips** \u2014 resistances, intrinsics, commons, extras, uniques and\nultimates, all six classes.\n\n**140 species** \u2014 all **68** from Tensura: Reincarnated, plus 72 from Ascension,\nSlimeThroneExtras and Jeremis Tensura.\n\nSkills from an addon you do not have simply stay silent. Nothing breaks, Great\nSage just never has a reason to name them. Subtitles in **English and French**,\ntimed from the audio itself.\n\n---\n\n## Settings\n\nEverything can be turned off, most of it can be tuned.\n\n| Setting | What it does |\n|---|---|\n| `compactSkillAnnounce` | Quiet corner mode instead of full screen. **Off by default** |\n| `enableTips` | The thirty spontaneous comments |\n| `tipQuietTicks` | Minimum silence between comments \u2014 companion or parrot |\n| `announcedTiers` | Which skill classes trigger an announce |\n| `skillBlacklist` | Skills that never get announced |\n| `showWithHiddenHud` | Keeps announcements visible under F1, for recording |\n| `darkenStrength` | How dark the screen gets, or 0 for not at all |\n| `enableVoice` / `enableOverlay` | Voice and visuals, independently |\n| `needGreatSage` | Gamerule: require the Great Sage skill for any of it |\n\n---\n\n## Requirements\n\n- Minecraft **1.21.1**\n- **NeoForge** 21.1.0+\n- **Tensura: Reincarnated** 2.0.0.0+, with ManasCore and Architectury\n\nAddons are optional \u2014 the mod adapts to whatever is loaded.\n\n---\n\n## Bonus\n\n**Reason-Destroying Sword, Venuzdonoa** \u2014 a Unique skill. Activating it drives\nthe blade up through the ground in front of you until it stands planted, with\ndebris and a low impact. Pure set piece for now, no combat effect. Nothing grants\nit automatically, so if you only want the announcements you can simply never\nlearn it.\n\n---\n\n## PS\n\nIt's the first Minecraft mod I've ever made, so expect bugs.\n\nBug reports and missing lines are genuinely useful. If a skill announces with a\nsilent gap where its name should be, the clip just isn't recorded yet \u2014 adding it\ntakes minutes.\n\nAll voice clips are extracted from *That Time I Got Reincarnated as a Slime*. I\nclaim no ownership over them.", "body_url": null, "published": "2026-08-13T21:20:01.022783Z", "updated": "2026-08-13T21:23:13.254126Z", "approved": "2026-09-24T17:52:53.252924Z", "queued": "2026-08-13T21:25:46.687491Z", "status": "approved", "requested_status": "approved", "moderator_message": null, "license": {"id": "LicenseRef-All-Rights-Reserved", "name": "", "url": null}, "downloads": 9, "followers": 0, "categories": ["game-mechanics"], "additional_categories": ["magic", "utility"], "loaders": ["neoforge"], "versions": ["SEhfkQVK"], "icon_url": "https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/roJlZcNx/25e99d9329b03422a6f8779740d62393ed2ced9a_96.webp", "raw_icon_url": "https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/roJlZcNx/25e99d9329b03422a6f8779740d62393ed2ced9a.png", "issues_url": null, "source_url": null, "wiki_url": null, "discord_url": null, "donation_urls": [], "gallery": [], "color": 4205865, "thread_id": "vPQGbEXU", "monetization_status": "monetized"}, {"client_side": "required", "server_side": "unsupported", "game_versions": ["1.20.1", "1.21.1"], "environment": ["client_only"], "id": "DUCu3Gg9", "slug": "qio-sync", "project_type": "mod", "team": "W7BmYfAp", "organization": null, "title": "QIO Sync", "description": "Adds configurable search synchronization in Mekanism's QIO storage interface for JEI or EMI, along with QOL improvements to recipe handling.", "body": "### QIO Sync is a client-side QOL mod for [Mekanism's](https://modrinth.com/mod/mekanism) QIO storage interface\n\nIt adds search synchronization inspired by [Refined Storage](https://modrinth.com/mod/refined-storage) and improves how [EMI](https://modrinth.com/mod/emi) or [JEI](https://modrinth.com/mod/jei) recipes are transferred into QIO's three crafting windows.\n\n### Search synchronization\n\n\u00a0A button in the QIO interface lets you choose how its search bar interacts with EMI or JEI:\n\n- OFF: QIO and recipe-viewer searches remain independent\n- 1W: Typing in QIO also updates the EMI or JEI search box\n- 2W: Typing in either search box updates the other\n\n### Improved QIO recipe transfer\nWhen using JEI or EMI's Fill Recipe button (+):\n- Automatically opens a QIO crafting window when necessary\n- Prioritizes empty crafting grids\n- Uses all three available QIO crafting windows\n- Replaces occupied grids in a round-robin pattern if every grid is in use\n\n### Forge 1.20.1 improvements\n\nThe Forge version provides several features from newer versions of Mekanism:\n- Fixes EMI recipe transfer and the Fill Recipe button in QIO\n- Fixes EMI recipe and usage keybinds while hovering over items stored in QIO\n- Prevents EMI recipe screens from closing QIO crafting windows unexpectedly\n- Adds a QIO/INV option for deciding where items displaced by a new crafting recipe are sent\n- Adds a GRID/QIO option for deciding whether items shift-clicked from the player's inventory go into the open crafting grid or get stored in the current QIO frequency\n- Adds extra auto-selected search modes which let you begin typing into a search box immediately upon opening QIO's interface\n\n### Installation and configuration\n\nQIO Sync is entirely client-side. **It does not need to be installed on a server.** Install it in the client's mods folder alongside [Mekanism](https://modrinth.com/mod/mekanism) and [EMI](https://modrinth.com/mod/emi) or [JEI](https://modrinth.com/mod/jei) (or both).\n\nThe UI behavior options added by this mod are saved in qiosync-client.toml. The settings are applied globally to every QIO interface accessed by the player.", "body_url": null, "published": "2026-08-18T20:44:31.167205Z", "updated": "2026-09-21T16:54:29.802746Z", "approved": "2026-09-24T18:17:07.943577Z", "queued": "2026-08-18T20:56:02.556738Z", "status": "approved", "requested_status": "approved", "moderator_message": null, "license": {"id": "LicenseRef-All-Rights-Reserved", "name": "", "url": null}, "downloads": 3, "followers": 0, "categories": ["storage", "technology", "utility"], "additional_categories": [], "loaders": ["forge", "neoforge"], "versions": ["fRPowDY1", "A4T1DUqq", "XZToODXh", "ZPridSsy"], "icon_url": "https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/DUCu3Gg9/6365b78710d19d5633cd482e924ec3a8fdd78bec_96.webp", "raw_icon_url": "https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/DUCu3Gg9/6365b78710d19d5633cd482e924ec3a8fdd78bec.png", "issues_url": null, "source_url": null, "wiki_url": null, "discord_url": null, "donation_urls": [], "gallery": [{"url": "https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/DUCu3Gg9/images/20012632a05573b451a81d3b70c58f94d21fa629_350.webp", "raw_url": "https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/DUCu3Gg9/images/20012632a05573b451a81d3b70c58f94d21fa629.png", "featured": false, "title": "Search sync disabled", "description": "QIO and EMI/JEI searches are independent", "created": "2026-08-18T20:49:20.591567Z", "ordering": 1}, {"url": "https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/DUCu3Gg9/images/b5ff26af284e6fa15aef7e12d61d6c224e779f7a_350.webp", "raw_url": "https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/DUCu3Gg9/images/b5ff26af284e6fa15aef7e12d61d6c224e779f7a.png", "featured": false, "title": "One-way sync", "description": "Typing in QIO also searches EMI/JEI", "created": "2026-08-18T20:50:07.861872Z", "ordering": 2}, {"url": "https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/DUCu3Gg9/images/9025199a6a0e8a0304301a4908aa00f6449d7d6d_350.webp", "raw_url": "https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/DUCu3Gg9/images/9025199a6a0e8a0304301a4908aa00f6449d7d6d.png", "featured": true, "title": "Two-way sync", "description": "Typing in either search field updates the other", "created": "2026-08-18T20:50:49.529605Z", "ordering": 3}], "color": 461580, "thread_id": "jhir3Yhb", "monetization_status": "monetized"}, {"client_side": "required", "server_side": "unsupported", "game_versions": ["1.21.11"], "environment": ["client_only"], "id": "ieGGHGLA", "slug": "pristine", "project_type": "mod", "team": "ODst9zlZ", "organization": null, "title": "Pristine", "description": "Mining focused utilities and QoL for Hypixel Skyblock.", "body": "# Pristine\n\nPristine is an endgame mining mod for Hypixel SkyBlock, focused on unique Glacite Tunnels and mineshafting utilities.\n\n## Setup Guide\n\nEnsure Fabric API and Fabric Language Kotlin are downloaded.\n\nClick right shift or type /pristine (/ps) to open the gui. \n\nThere you will be prompted to either to start with all features un-toggled or with the defaults on. You can always untoggle all settings in the Settings tab. The reset icon to the right of the Configure button allows you to return to the default settings at any time, even if you untoggle everything.\n\nClick **Configure** in the bottom left to move and position your HUDs.\n\nYou can further tweak popups and other cosmetics in the Configure card, but you should be all set to get started.\n\n## Features\n\n<details>\n<summary>General Mining</summary>\n\n- Pickaxe Ability\n  - Widgetless, able to be used on non-mining islands without tablist and more accurate than tablist-based trackers\n- Gemstone Profit HUD\n- Efficiency Tracker\n- Wisp Cooldown\n- Wisp Radius Rendering\n- Skymall Tracker\n- Flowstate Tracker\n- Gemstone Highlight\n  - Tailor-made for gemstones, highlights the border of each gem instead of the whole block\n- Configure\n  - Move HUDs, change color, placement, and duration of popups, and more\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>Glacite Tunnels</summary>\n\n- Glacite Commissions HUD\n  - Image-based, true to the vanilla HUD design. Instantly updates instead of waiting for tablist\n- Pristine Display\n  - Hide, compact, or separate GUI\n- Spawning Stats\n  - Track shafts spawned, average spawn times, and how fast your last spawn was\n- Shafting Sessions\n  - Track nearly every stat and source of profit while shafting\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>Waypoints</summary>\n\n- Ordered and Unordered Waypoints\n- Auto-Load Waypoints on Shaft\n- Configurable Waypoint Types\n- Custom Route Manager\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>Mineshafts</summary>\n\n- Shaft PBs\n  - Track the amount of gemstones you mine per shaft\n- History\n  - View your saved personal bests and sessions. PBs are filterable by corpse count, HOTM abilities, and mining event\n- Corpse Popup\n  - View corpse count and type, Mayhem ability, and mining event when entering a new shaft\n- Mute Corpses\n  - Mute the Organ Donor accessory line\n- Track Last Lobby\n  - Tracks the lobby you last spawned a shaft in\n- Time Left In Shaft\n  - Accurate, quick calculation\n- Fines In Shaft\n- Maniacs Killed HUD\n- Shaft Cooldown\n  - Avoid re-entering too quickly\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>QoL</summary>\n\n- Performance HUD\n  - Ping, FPS, and TPS in one place\n- Now Playing\n  - Track what song you're playing and easily pause, skip, or go to the previous song with a keybind\n- Lobby Marker\n- Timers\n- Slot Locking\n- Consumables Countdown\n  - Track mining consumables and get reminders before they expire\n- Lobby Day\n- Transfer Cooldown\n  - Dynamically change the delay in case of an update\n\n</details>\n", "body_url": null, "published": "2026-06-07T05:01:26.131123Z", "updated": "2026-06-13T04:52:52.629500Z", "approved": "2026-09-24T19:47:11.784177Z", "queued": "2026-08-17T19:34:56.337766Z", "status": "approved", "requested_status": "approved", "moderator_message": null, "license": {"id": "Apache-2.0", "name": "Apache License 2.0", "url": null}, "downloads": 8, "followers": 0, "categories": [], "additional_categories": [], "loaders": ["fabric"], "versions": ["fpfbi96m"], "icon_url": "https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/ieGGHGLA/6e59a130970ed6a9da253fb6a466ccfc1310ef06_96.webp", "raw_icon_url": "https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/ieGGHGLA/6e59a130970ed6a9da253fb6a466ccfc1310ef06.png", "issues_url": null, "source_url": null, "wiki_url": null, "discord_url": null, "donation_urls": [], "gallery": [{"url": "https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/ieGGHGLA/images/14e3ad5e171a51dbad46dd7ad8baa8ae72911775.png", "raw_url": "https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/ieGGHGLA/images/14e3ad5e171a51dbad46dd7ad8baa8ae72911775.png", "featured": false, "title": null, "description": null, "created": "2026-06-13T04:53:35.248824Z", "ordering": 0}], "color": 263172, "thread_id": "DPoL5fkV", "monetization_status": "monetized"}, {"client_side": "required", "server_side": "required", "game_versions": ["1.21", "1.21.1", "1.21.2", "1.21.3", "1.21.4", "1.21.5", "1.21.6", "1.21.7", "1.21.8", "1.21.9", "1.21.10", "1.21.11", "26.1", "26.1.1", "26.1.2", "26.2"], "environment": ["client_and_server"], "id": "dwS7is1Q", "slug": "livevillages", "project_type": "mod", "team": "Phs3EQBL", "organization": null, "title": "LiveVillages", "description": "Turn your TikTok LIVE audience into villagers that build and populate your Minecraft world.", "body": "**Turn your live stream into a village. Every gift builds a house.**\n\nLiveVillages is a NeoForge mod that grows a village in real time from the gifts your viewers\nsend you on a live stream. Each donation places a house, moves in a villager named after the\ndonor, and wires the new home into the town with a real road, a lamp post and a sign.\nNothing is pre-built: the town grows organically, house by house, while your audience watches.\n\nBuilt for TikTok LIVE, and usable by hand even without a live running.\nWorks in single-player and on a dedicated server alike \u2014 the connection just lives in\nwhichever player's client runs `/lv tiktok connect`, so that player needs the mod\ninstalled. For a version where the connection runs on the server itself (no client\ninstall for anyone), see the LiveVillages plugin for Paper servers, on\n[Hangar](https://hangar.papermc.io/Vutoquii/LiveVillages),\n[Modrinth](https://modrinth.com/project/livevillages) or\n[SpigotMC](https://www.spigotmc.org/resources/livevillages-tiktok-live-donor-villages.137603/).\n\n> **Two Minecraft versions, one mod.** LiveVillages is published for both **1.21.1** and\n> **26.x**. Grab the file tagged for the version you run \u2014 CurseForge separates them so you\n> never install the wrong one. If you're upgrading an existing 1.21.1 world to 26.x, your\n> villages come with you automatically: the mod finds and migrates them the first time you\n> load the world, no extra steps.\n\n> **Platform status:** TikTok LIVE is the only platform connected right now. YouTube Live and\n> Twitch support is in development. In the meantime, the manual commands already work with\n> any source of events \u2014 including those two.\n\n---\n\n## How it works\n\nThere are two ways to place houses, and they both go through the same door in the code, so\nthey behave identically:\n\n1. **By hand** \u2014 you (or an authorized moderator) run a command: `/lv house add` for a\n   quick placement, or `/lv house donate` to simulate a specific gift and let the mod pick\n   the house. Great for testing, giveaways, and for rewarding people outside the stream.\n2. **Connected to TikTok LIVE** \u2014 `/lv tiktok connect <username> <village>` listens to your\n   live and places a house every time a gift arrives. YouTube and Twitch are on the roadmap.\n\nThe mod decides *which* house a gift builds from a configurable gift table, so a small gift\ngives a small house and a money gun gives the good one.\n\n---\n\n## Features\n\n**Organic town growth**\n- Houses are scattered around a central plaza with randomized angle and radius, and rejected\n  if they land too close to another house, on water or lava, or on top of an existing road.\n- Every plot is levelled to the true average ground height underneath it \u2014 trees, grass, snow\n  and water are ignored, so a house on a slope sits properly instead of floating or sinking.\n\n**Roads that actually make sense**\n- Paths are generated with A\\* pathfinding over a cost map, so roads bend around obstacles\n  instead of bulldozing through them.\n- Automatic terracing on slopes, bridges over water, lamp posts with hanging lanterns along\n  the way, and decoration.\n\n**Nothing is destructive**\n- Every house records the previous state of every block it changed. Removing a house restores\n  the terrain exactly as it was, in reverse order.\n\n**Multiple villages**\n- Create as many towns as you want, mark one as active, open and close them to new arrivals,\n  rename, teleport to, regenerate or delete them independently.\n\n**House styles you can extend without recompiling**\n- Houses are `.nbt` structures grouped into skins (a theme) and models (a tier). The catalog\n  lives in a JSON config file, so you can add your own builds \u2014 plaza, houses, lamp post \u2014 and\n  map them to gift tiers yourself.\n\n**Villager management**\n- Each house gets its own villager with a workstation and a sign carrying the donor's name.\n  Villager AI can be paused per village (useful during a long stream), and a revive command\n  brings back anyone who died. `/lv house regenerate` reuses the existing villager instead\n  of spawning a duplicate, and keeps their assigned profession instead of re-rolling it.\n\n**Built-in GUI**\n- `/lv gui` opens an in-game catalog of every command with a form for each one, so you don't\n  have to memorize the syntax mid-stream.\n\n**Permissions**\n- Three levels: admin, authorized users (by UUID, granted in-game), and everyone else. Hand\n  a moderator the controls without handing them your server.\n\n**Localization**\n- Fully translated into English and Spanish. Every player sees the mod in their own Minecraft\n  language setting.\n\n---\n\n## Requirements\n\nPick the file that matches your Minecraft version \u2014 CurseForge tags each download, so the\napp installs the right one automatically.\n\n| Minecraft | NeoForge | Java |\n|---|---|---|\n| **1.21.1** | 21.1.x | 21 |\n| **26.x** | 26.1.x | 25 |\n\n- For the TikTok LIVE connection only: the companion library mod (listed as a dependency \u2014\n  the CurseForge app installs and updates it for you). Manual placement works without it.\n\n---\n\n## Commands\n\nRoot command is `/lv` (`/livevillage` works as an alias). Everything requires operator level 2.\n\n### Villages\n```\n/lv village create <name> [skin]      Create a village where you stand\n/lv village list                      List every village\n/lv village setactive <name>          Choose which village receives donations\n/lv village tp <name>                 Teleport to a village\n/lv village rename <old> <new>        Rename a village\n/lv village open|close <name>         Allow or stop new houses\n/lv village ai <name> on|off          Pause or resume villager AI\n/lv village forceload <name> on|off   Keep chunks loaded while building\n/lv village regenerate <name>         Rebuild roads and decoration\n/lv village delete <name>             Delete the village and restore the terrain\n```\n\n### Houses\n```\n/lv house add <model> <donor>                   Place a house in the active village\n/lv house addto <village> <model> <donor>       Place a house in a specific village\n/lv house donate <village> <giftId> <coins> <gift>|<donor>\n                                                Simulate a real donation\n/lv house list                                  List houses with their owners\n/lv house rename <n> <name>                     Change the name on the sign\n/lv house tp <n>                                Teleport to a house\n/lv house revive                                Bring back missing villagers\n/lv house regenerate <n>                        Rebuild a house\n/lv house remove <n>                            Remove it and restore the terrain\n```\n\n### Gifts\n```\n/lv gift list                                   Show the gift to house table\n/lv gift set monedas <coins> <model>            Map a coin value to a house model\n/lv gift set id <giftId> <model>                Map a specific gift ID to a model\n/lv gift set tramo <min> <max> <model>          Map a coin range to a model\n/lv gift set nombre <model> <gift>              Map a gift by name\n/lv gift remove <n>                             Delete a rule\n/lv gift test <giftId> <coins> <name>           Dry run a gift without placing anything\n/lv gift log on|off|show                        Log incoming gifts to find their IDs\n```\n\n### Models and skins\n```\n/lv model list                                  List every model\n/lv model info <model>                          Details of one model\n/lv model add <id> <skin> <coins> <structure>   Register a new house model\n/lv model remove <id>                           Remove a model\n/lv model skin add <name> <lift> <plaza> <post> Register a new skin\n/lv model skin remove <name>                    Remove a skin\n```\n\n### TikTok LIVE\n```\n/lv tiktok connect <username> <village>         Connect to a live and start listening\n/lv tiktok status                               Connection status\n/lv tiktok disconnect                           Stop listening\n/lv tiktok diag                                 Diagnose the library setup\n```\n\n### System\n```\n/lv gui                                         Open the command catalog\n/lv reload                                      Reload the config files\n/lv perm grant|revoke <player>                  Manage authorized users\n/lv perm list                                   List authorized users\n```\n\n---\n\n## Configuration\n\nTwo JSON files are created in your `config/` folder on first run and can be reloaded live\nwith `/lv reload`:\n\n- `livevillage-regalos.json` \u2014 the gift-to-house table.\n- `livevillage-modelos.json` \u2014 the catalog of skins and house models.\n\nA broken JSON file never takes the server down: the mod warns and keeps the previous values.\n\n---\n\n## Notes\n\n- **Not affiliated with, endorsed by, or sponsored by TikTok or ByteDance.** TikTok is a\n  trademark of its respective owner and is referenced here only to describe what the mod\n  connects to.\n- The live connection relies on a third-party, unofficial library\n  ([TikTokLiveJava](https://github.com/jwdeveloper/TikTok-Live-Java) by jwdeveloper, MIT).\n  It is not an official API, so it can break temporarily when the platform changes something.\n  Manual placement is unaffected.\n- If you run a public or paid server, you are responsible for making sure how you reward\n  donors complies with the Minecraft Usage Guidelines. This mod is a building tool; how you\n  use it is on you.\n\n---\n\n## Support\n\nLiveVillages is free. If it's useful to you and you'd like to help keep it going, you can\nleave a tip here: **[paypal.me/josstv77](https://www.paypal.me/josstv77)**.\nCompletely optional \u2014 the mod isn't gated behind it in any way.\n\n---\n\n## Feedback\n\nBug reports and feature requests: please leave a comment on this page.\n\n", "body_url": null, "published": "2026-08-01T22:50:45.397393Z", "updated": "2026-08-17T08:30:27.993806Z", "approved": "2026-09-24T18:22:06.367528Z", "queued": "2026-08-17T08:36:05.813800Z", "status": "approved", "requested_status": "approved", "moderator_message": null, "license": {"id": "MIT", "name": "MIT License", "url": null}, "downloads": 11, "followers": 0, "categories": ["utility"], "additional_categories": ["game-mechanics", "minigame"], "loaders": ["fabric", "neoforge", "paper"], "versions": ["8tsuRnaa", "Z3E9cMFm", "isMSxFZF"], "icon_url": "https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/dwS7is1Q/d0af0a0c6940da4ab2519500aff9e3c1412d97d6_96.webp", "raw_icon_url": "https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/dwS7is1Q/d0af0a0c6940da4ab2519500aff9e3c1412d97d6.webp", "issues_url": null, "source_url": null, "wiki_url": null, "discord_url": null, "donation_urls": [{"id": "paypal", "platform": "Paypal", "url": "https://www.paypal.com/paypalme/josstv77"}], "gallery": [{"url": "https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/dwS7is1Q/images/9a31f8ba4dc3002c9f4e063f235416332411168c_350.webp", "raw_url": "https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/dwS7is1Q/images/9a31f8ba4dc3002c9f4e063f235416332411168c.jpeg", "featured": false, "title": null, "description": null, "created": "2026-08-02T02:45:02.898847Z", "ordering": 0}, {"url": "https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/dwS7is1Q/images/d50949f45ffcfe80a3c5488035397a6608daca93_350.webp", "raw_url": "https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/dwS7is1Q/images/d50949f45ffcfe80a3c5488035397a6608daca93.jpeg", "featured": false, "title": null, "description": null, "created": "2026-08-02T02:44:57.390031Z", "ordering": 0}, {"url": "https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/dwS7is1Q/images/fd04bfac6a5a169b2c14e267b7e4421c015c356a_350.webp", "raw_url": "https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/dwS7is1Q/images/fd04bfac6a5a169b2c14e267b7e4421c015c356a.jpeg", "featured": true, "title": null, "description": null, "created": "2026-08-02T02:44:51.049750Z", "ordering": 0}], "color": 2827816, "thread_id": "be65IjLA", "monetization_status": "monetized"}, {"client_side": "required", "server_side": "unsupported", "game_versions": ["26.2"], "environment": ["client_only"], "id": "TvZ8ryqU", "slug": "aechronis-map-overlay", "project_type": "mod", "team": "sYQ1Xh97", "organization": null, "title": "Aechronis Nation Overlay", "description": "This project renders live nation borders onto xaero's minimap and world map for the minecraft server Aechronis", "body": "**Aechronis Nation Overlay**\n\nA live map overlay for the [Aechronis](https://aechronis.net/) Minecraft server. It shows nation nodes on your minimap and world map, so you can see who owns what at a glance.\n\n**This mod only works on the Aechronis server.** On any other server, or in singleplayer, it does nothing.\n\n## Features\n\n- Nodes shown in each nation's color, right on the map\n- Town and nation names labeled at their locations\n- Resource-rich land marked and labeled\n- Ports and other buildings marked\n- Live war updates \u2014 see territory change hands in real time during a siege\n\n## Requirements\n\n- Fabric API\n- [XaeroPlus](https://modrinth.com/mod/xaeroplus)\n- [Xaero's Minimap](https://modrinth.com/mod/xaeros-minimap)\n- [Xaero's World Map](https://modrinth.com/mod/xaeros-world-map)\n- Cloth Config\n- Mod Menu (optional, for in-game settings)\n\n## Links\n\n- Discord: https://discord.gg/pbPSV3KtDp\n- Source code: https://github.com/DCFiendish/Aechronis-Map-Mod\n\n## Support\n\nFound a bug or have a feature request? Please report it on Discord or GitHub \u2014 not in Modrinth comments/reviews.", "body_url": null, "published": "2026-08-17T01:07:04.578867Z", "updated": "2026-08-21T16:59:21.346919Z", "approved": "2026-09-24T18:20:41.913204Z", "queued": "2026-08-17T02:07:27.645938Z", "status": "approved", "requested_status": "approved", "moderator_message": null, "license": {"id": "Apache-2.0", "name": "Apache License 2.0", "url": "https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0"}, "downloads": 1, "followers": 1, "categories": ["utility"], "additional_categories": [], "loaders": ["fabric"], "versions": ["iYnZG33A", "vmmwDOgp", "TvtZ2ERG", "xqBScfOr", "BO9a6OUW", "gX5JRaIr", "unOk7vdo", "F6x2HSUr", "IZnSRDci", "WBJ3u7Ie", "suLl3Rvn"], "icon_url": "https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/TvZ8ryqU/2219e5090d08b95f0a4e54bfccc51337231fdca7_96.webp", "raw_icon_url": "https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/TvZ8ryqU/2219e5090d08b95f0a4e54bfccc51337231fdca7.png", "issues_url": null, "source_url": "https://github.com/DCFiendish/Aechronis-Map-Mod/", "wiki_url": null, "discord_url": null, "donation_urls": [], "gallery": [], "color": 13744532, "thread_id": "FmidyvLQ", "monetization_status": "monetized"}, {"client_side": "optional", "server_side": "optional", "game_versions": ["1.8", "1.8.1", "1.8.2", "1.8.3", "1.8.4", "1.8.5", "1.8.6", "1.8.7", "1.8.8", "1.8.9", "1.9", "1.9.1", "1.9.2", "1.9.3", "1.9.4", "1.10", "1.10.1", "1.10.2", "1.11", "1.11.1", "1.11.2", "1.12", "1.12.1", "1.12.2", "1.13", "1.13.1", "1.13.2", "1.14", "1.14.1", "1.14.2", "1.14.3", "1.14.4", "1.15", "1.15.1", "1.15.2", "1.16", "1.16.1", "1.16.2", "1.16.3", "1.16.4", "1.16.5", "1.17", "1.17.1", "1.18", "1.18.1", "1.18.2", "1.19", "1.19.1", "1.19.2", "1.19.3", "1.19.4", "1.20", "1.20.1", "1.20.2", "1.20.3", "1.20.4", "1.20.5", "1.20.6", "1.21", "1.21.1", "1.21.2", "1.21.3", "1.21.4", "1.21.5", "1.21.6", "1.21.7", "1.21.8", "1.21.9", "1.21.10", "1.21.11", "26.1", "26.1.1", "26.1.2", "26.2"], "environment": ["client_or_server"], "id": "ZMwajBP3", "slug": "universalfml", "project_type": "mod", "team": "I3KbTchH", "organization": null, "title": "Universal FML", "description": "An easy way to make Forge mods for both 1.8-1.12 and 1.13+", "body": "An easy way for mod developers to make Forge mods for both 1.8-1.12 and 1.13+.\n\n# Players:\nThis mod does **NOTHING** on either the client or server. You do not need to install it. It is for developers only.\n\n# Developers:\nThis mod defines a `net.minecraftforge.fml.common.Mod` annotation that contains both the legacy (1.8-1.12) and modern (1.13+) fields. This allows you to load one entrypoint in both legacy and modern forge, without having to make a split buildscript or deal with projects like Stonecutter.\n\n# Why?\nI wanted to mixin into other mods (namely Essential) on 1.8 through 1.20.\n\n# Fabric/Neo?\nFabric uses fabric.mod.json to load entrypoints, which is intentionally kept backwards-compatible.\nNeoforge uses `net.neoforged.fml.common.Mod`, which you should be able to add (to a seperate class) and load with no issue.\n\n# Usage\nShort answer: `@Mod(value = \"mymodid\", modid = \"mymodid\", useMetadata = true)`, then put all of your metadata into `mcmod.info` and `mods.toml`.  \nLong answer: see the [GitHub](https://github.com/cootshk/UniversalFML).", "body_url": null, "published": "2026-08-18T01:11:11.800454Z", "updated": "2026-08-18T04:20:27.807294Z", "approved": "2026-09-24T19:51:30.525176Z", "queued": "2026-08-18T04:26:23.784259Z", "status": "approved", "requested_status": "approved", "moderator_message": null, "license": {"id": "LGPL-2.1-only", "name": "GNU Lesser General Public License v2.1 only", "url": "https://github.com/MinecraftForge/MinecraftForge/blob/26.2/LICENSE.txt"}, "downloads": 3, "followers": 0, "categories": ["utility"], "additional_categories": ["cursed", "library"], "loaders": ["forge"], "versions": ["radrnuNz"], "icon_url": null, "raw_icon_url": null, "issues_url": "https://github.com/cootshk/universalfml/issues", "source_url": "https://github.com/cootshk/universalfml", "wiki_url": null, "discord_url": "https://cootshk.dev/discord", "donation_urls": [], "gallery": [], "color": null, "thread_id": "XwHger7g", "monetization_status": "monetized"}, {"client_side": "required", "server_side": "unsupported", "game_versions": ["26.1.1"], "environment": ["client_only"], "id": "clgug7NI", "slug": "the-draftout-russifier", "project_type": "mod", "team": "flb6ePk7", "organization": null, "title": "The Draftout Russifier", "description": "Draftout Russianizer, translation of the Draftout mod into Russian. \u0420\u0443\u0441\u0438\u0444\u0438\u043a\u0430\u0442\u043e\u0440 \u0434\u043b\u044f Draftout", "body": "# The Draftout Russifier\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary><b>\u041e\u043f\u0438\u0441\u0430\u043d\u0438\u0435 \u043d\u0430 \u0440\u0443\u0441\u0441\u043a\u043e\u043c \u044f\u0437\u044b\u043a\u0435 (\u041d\u0430\u0436\u043c\u0438\u0442\u0435, \u0447\u0442\u043e\u0431\u044b \u0440\u0430\u0437\u0432\u0435\u0440\u043d\u0443\u0442\u044c)</b></summary>\n\n<br>\n\n# \u041e\u043f\u0438\u0441\u0430\u043d\u0438\u0435 \u043c\u043e\u0434\u0430 (Russian)\n\n**The Draftout Russifier** \u2014 \u044d\u0442\u043e \u043e\u0442\u0434\u0435\u043b\u044c\u043d\u044b\u0439 Fabric-\u043c\u043e\u0434, \u043f\u0440\u0435\u0434\u043e\u0441\u0442\u0430\u0432\u043b\u044f\u044e\u0449\u0438\u0439 \u043f\u043e\u043b\u043d\u0443\u044e \u0438 \u043a\u0430\u0447\u0435\u0441\u0442\u0432\u0435\u043d\u043d\u0443\u044e \u0440\u0443\u0441\u0438\u0444\u0438\u043a\u0430\u0446\u0438\u044e \u0434\u043b\u044f \u0441\u043e\u0440\u0435\u0432\u043d\u043e\u0432\u0430\u0442\u0435\u043b\u044c\u043d\u043e\u0433\u043e Minecraft-\u043c\u043e\u0434\u0430 **[Draftout](https://modrinth.com/mod/draftout)**.\n\n### \u2753 \u0417\u0430\u0447\u0435\u043c \u043d\u0443\u0436\u0435\u043d \u043e\u0442\u0434\u0435\u043b\u044c\u043d\u044b\u0439 \u043c\u043e\u0434, \u0430 \u043d\u0435 \u0440\u0435\u0441\u0443\u0440\u0441\u043f\u0430\u043a?\n\u0412\u043e \u0432\u0440\u0435\u043c\u044f \u0441\u043e\u0440\u0435\u0432\u043d\u043e\u0432\u0430\u0442\u0435\u043b\u044c\u043d\u044b\u0445 \u043c\u0430\u0442\u0447\u0435\u0439 \u0432 \u043c\u043e\u0434\u0435 Draftout \u043f\u0440\u0438\u043d\u0443\u0434\u0438\u0442\u0435\u043b\u044c\u043d\u043e \u043e\u0442\u043a\u043b\u044e\u0447\u0430\u044e\u0442\u0441\u044f \u0432\u0441\u0435 \u043f\u043e\u043b\u044c\u0437\u043e\u0432\u0430\u0442\u0435\u043b\u044c\u0441\u043a\u0438\u0435 \u0440\u0435\u0441\u0443\u0440\u0441\u043f\u0430\u043a\u0438. \u0414\u0430\u043d\u043d\u044b\u0439 \u043c\u043e\u0434 \u0438\u043d\u0442\u0435\u0433\u0440\u0438\u0440\u0443\u0435\u0442 \u0440\u0443\u0441\u0441\u043a\u0438\u0439 \u044f\u0437\u044b\u043a \u043d\u0430\u043f\u0440\u044f\u043c\u0443\u044e \u0432 \u043a\u043b\u0438\u0435\u043d\u0442 \u0438\u0433\u0440\u044b, \u0431\u043b\u0430\u0433\u043e\u0434\u0430\u0440\u044f \u0447\u0435\u043c\u0443 \u0432\u0435\u0441\u044c \u0438\u043d\u0442\u0435\u0440\u0444\u0435\u0439\u0441 \u0438 \u0446\u0435\u043b\u0438 \u043e\u0441\u0442\u0430\u044e\u0442\u0441\u044f \u043d\u0430 \u0440\u0443\u0441\u0441\u043a\u043e\u043c \u044f\u0437\u044b\u043a\u0435 \u0434\u0430\u0436\u0435 \u0432\u043e \u0432\u0440\u0435\u043c\u044f \u043c\u0430\u0442\u0447\u0435\u0439.\n\n### \u2728 \u0427\u0442\u043e \u043f\u0435\u0440\u0435\u0432\u0435\u0434\u0435\u043d\u043e (639 \u0441\u0442\u0440\u043e\u043a):\n- **\u0412\u0441\u0435 \u0446\u0435\u043b\u0438 (Goals):** \u0442\u043e\u0447\u043d\u044b\u0439 \u0438 \u043f\u043e\u043d\u044f\u0442\u043d\u044b\u0439 \u043f\u0435\u0440\u0435\u0432\u043e\u0434 \u0432\u0441\u0435\u0445 \u0443\u0441\u043b\u043e\u0432\u0438\u0439 (\u0434\u043e\u0441\u0442\u0438\u0436\u0435\u043d\u0438\u044f, \u043c\u043e\u0431\u044b, \u0440\u0430\u0437\u043c\u043d\u043e\u0436\u0435\u043d\u0438\u0435, \u043a\u0440\u0430\u0444\u0442\u044b, \u0437\u0435\u043b\u044c\u044f, \u0443\u0440\u043e\u043d \u0438 \u0434\u0440.) \u0441 \u0441\u043e\u0431\u043b\u044e\u0434\u0435\u043d\u0438\u0435\u043c \u043a\u0430\u043d\u043e\u043d\u0438\u0447\u0435\u0441\u043a\u0438\u0445 \u043d\u0430\u0437\u0432\u0430\u043d\u0438\u0439 \u043e\u0444\u0438\u0446\u0438\u0430\u043b\u044c\u043d\u043e\u0439 \u0440\u0443\u0441\u0441\u043a\u043e\u0439 \u0432\u0435\u0440\u0441\u0438\u0438 Minecraft (*\u0442\u0438\u0445\u043e\u043d\u044f, \u043b\u0430\u0432\u043e\u043c\u0435\u0440\u043a\u0430, \u043a\u0430\u0434\u0430\u0432\u0440, \u0437\u0438\u043c\u043e\u0433\u043e\u0440, \u0445\u0440\u0430\u043d\u0438\u0442\u0435\u043b\u044c, \u043a\u0430\u043c\u0435\u043d\u0438\u0441\u0442\u0430\u044f \u0437\u0435\u043c\u043b\u044f, \u043d\u0435\u0437\u0435\u0440\u0438\u0442\u043e\u0432\u044b\u0439 \u043b\u043e\u043c, \u043a\u0443\u0437\u043d\u0435\u0447\u043d\u044b\u0439 \u0448\u0430\u0431\u043b\u043e\u043d* \u0438 \u0442.\u0434.).\n- **\u0412\u043d\u0443\u0442\u0440\u0438\u0438\u0433\u0440\u043e\u0432\u043e\u0439 \u0440\u0435\u0434\u0430\u043a\u0442\u043e\u0440 \u043f\u0435\u0440\u0435\u0432\u043e\u0434\u0430:** \u0432\u043e\u0437\u043c\u043e\u0436\u043d\u043e\u0441\u0442\u044c \u0440\u0435\u0434\u0430\u043a\u0442\u0438\u0440\u043e\u0432\u0430\u0442\u044c \u043b\u044e\u0431\u044b\u0435 \u0441\u0442\u0440\u043e\u043a\u0438 \u043f\u0440\u044f\u043c\u043e \u0432 \u0433\u043b\u0430\u0432\u043d\u043e\u043c \u043c\u0435\u043d\u044e Minecraft \u0441 \u043c\u0433\u043d\u043e\u0432\u0435\u043d\u043d\u044b\u043c \u043f\u0440\u0438\u043c\u0435\u043d\u0435\u043d\u0438\u0435\u043c \u0431\u0435\u0437 \u043f\u0435\u0440\u0435\u0437\u0430\u043f\u0443\u0441\u043a\u0430 \u0438\u0433\u0440\u044b \u0438 \u0430\u0432\u0442\u043e\u0441\u043e\u0445\u0440\u0430\u043d\u0435\u043d\u0438\u0435\u043c \u0432 \u043a\u043e\u043d\u0444\u0438\u0433.\n- **\u041b\u043e\u0431\u0431\u0438 \u0438 \u0420\u0435\u0439\u0442\u0438\u043d\u0433:** \u0438\u043d\u0442\u0435\u0440\u0444\u0435\u0439\u0441 \u0441\u043e\u0437\u0434\u0430\u043d\u0438\u044f \u043b\u043e\u0431\u0431\u0438, \u043f\u0430\u0440\u0430\u043c\u0435\u0442\u0440\u044b \u0432\u0440\u0435\u043c\u0435\u043d\u0438, \u043e\u0432\u0435\u0440\u0442\u0430\u0439\u043c\u044b, \u0434\u043e\u0441\u043a\u0438, \u0444\u0438\u043b\u044c\u0442\u0440\u044b \u0438 \u0441\u0442\u0430\u0442\u0438\u0441\u0442\u0438\u043a\u0430.\n- **\u041a\u043e\u043d\u0441\u0442\u0440\u0443\u043a\u0442\u043e\u0440 \u0434\u043e\u0441\u043e\u043a (Board Builder):** \u0432\u0441\u0435 \u043f\u043e\u0434\u0441\u043a\u0430\u0437\u043a\u0438, \u043a\u043d\u043e\u043f\u043a\u0438 \u0441\u043e\u0445\u0440\u0430\u043d\u0435\u043d\u0438\u044f, \u0437\u0430\u0433\u0440\u0443\u0437\u043a\u0438 \u0438 \u043f\u043e\u0438\u0441\u043a\u0430 \u0446\u0435\u043b\u0435\u0439.\n- **\u0421\u0438\u0441\u0442\u0435\u043c\u0430 \u043f\u043e\u0432\u0442\u043e\u0440\u043e\u0432 (Replays):** \u0443\u043f\u0440\u0430\u0432\u043b\u0435\u043d\u0438\u0435 \u0432\u043e\u0441\u043f\u0440\u043e\u0438\u0437\u0432\u0435\u0434\u0435\u043d\u0438\u0435\u043c, \u043f\u0435\u0440\u0435\u043c\u043e\u0442\u043a\u0430, \u0441\u043b\u0435\u0434\u043e\u0432\u0430\u043d\u0438\u0435 \u0437\u0430 \u0438\u0433\u0440\u043e\u043a\u043e\u043c \u0438 \u043f\u0440\u043e\u0441\u043c\u043e\u0442\u0440 \u043c\u043e\u043c\u0435\u043d\u0442\u043e\u0432 \u0432\u044b\u043f\u043e\u043b\u043d\u0435\u043d\u0438\u044f \u0446\u0435\u043b\u0435\u0439.\n- **\u041d\u0430\u0441\u0442\u0440\u043e\u0439\u043a\u0438:** \u043f\u043e\u0437\u0438\u0446\u0438\u043e\u043d\u0438\u0440\u043e\u0432\u0430\u043d\u0438\u0435 \u0434\u043e\u0441\u043a\u0438, \u043c\u0430\u0441\u0448\u0442\u0430\u0431, \u043f\u043e\u0434\u0441\u0432\u0435\u0442\u043a\u0430 \u0432\u044b\u043f\u043e\u043b\u043d\u0435\u043d\u043d\u044b\u0445 \u0446\u0435\u043b\u0435\u0439 \u0438 \u0443\u0442\u0438\u043b\u0438\u0442\u044b.\n\n### \u0423\u0441\u0442\u0430\u043d\u043e\u0432\u043a\u0430\n1. \u0423\u0431\u0435\u0434\u0438\u0442\u0435\u0441\u044c, \u0447\u0442\u043e \u0443 \u0432\u0430\u0441 \u0443\u0441\u0442\u0430\u043d\u043e\u0432\u043b\u0435\u043d **Fabric Loader** \u0434\u043b\u044f Minecraft **26.1.1**.\n2. \u0423\u0441\u0442\u0430\u043d\u043e\u0432\u0438\u0442\u0435 \u043e\u0440\u0438\u0433\u0438\u043d\u0430\u043b\u044c\u043d\u044b\u0439 \u043c\u043e\u0434 **[Draftout](https://modrinth.com/mod/draftout)**\n3. \u0423\u0441\u0442\u0430\u043d\u043e\u0432\u0438\u0442\u0435 **The Draftout Russifier**\n4. \u0417\u0430\u043f\u0443\u0441\u0442\u0438\u0442\u0435 \u0438\u0433\u0440\u0443 \u0438 \u0432 \u043d\u0430\u0441\u0442\u0440\u043e\u0439\u043a\u0430\u0445 \u044f\u0437\u044b\u043a\u0430 \u0432\u044b\u0431\u0435\u0440\u0438\u0442\u0435 **\u0420\u0443\u0441\u0441\u043a\u0438\u0439 (\u0420\u043e\u0441\u0441\u0438\u044f)**.\n\n### \u26a0\ufe0f \u0412\u0430\u0436\u043d\u043e\u0435 \u043f\u0440\u0435\u0434\u0443\u043f\u0440\u0435\u0436\u0434\u0435\u043d\u0438\u0435 (Disclaimer) & \u041f\u0440\u0430\u0432\u0438\u043b\u0430 Draftout\n\u041f\u0435\u0440\u0435\u0434 \u0438\u0433\u0440\u043e\u0439 \u0432 \u0441\u043e\u0440\u0435\u0432\u043d\u043e\u0432\u0430\u0442\u0435\u043b\u044c\u043d\u043e\u043c \u0440\u0435\u0436\u0438\u043c\u0435 \u043e\u0437\u043d\u0430\u043a\u043e\u043c\u044c\u0442\u0435\u0441\u044c \u0441 [\u043e\u0444\u0438\u0446\u0438\u0430\u043b\u044c\u043d\u044b\u043c\u0438 \u043f\u0440\u0430\u0432\u0438\u043b\u0430\u043c\u0438 Draftout (\u043f\u0443\u043d\u043a\u0442 03: Mod rules)](https://draftoutmc.com/rules#mods).\n\n- **\u0421\u0442\u0430\u0442\u0443\u0441 \u043c\u043e\u0434\u0438\u0444\u0438\u043a\u0430\u0446\u0438\u0438:** \u0414\u0430\u043d\u043d\u044b\u0439 \u043f\u0440\u043e\u0435\u043a\u0442 \u044f\u0432\u043b\u044f\u0435\u0442\u0441\u044f \u043b\u044e\u0431\u0438\u0442\u0435\u043b\u044c\u0441\u043a\u043e\u0439 \u0444\u0430\u043d\u0430\u0442\u0441\u043a\u043e\u0439 \u043b\u043e\u043a\u0430\u043b\u0438\u0437\u0430\u0446\u0438\u0435\u0439 \u0438 **\u043d\u0435 \u043e\u0434\u043e\u0431\u0440\u0435\u043d \u043e\u0444\u0438\u0446\u0438\u0430\u043b\u044c\u043d\u043e \u043a\u043e\u043c\u0430\u043d\u0434\u043e\u0439 \u0440\u0430\u0437\u0440\u0430\u0431\u043e\u0442\u0447\u0438\u043a\u043e\u0432 Draftout**.\n- **\u041e\u0442\u043a\u0430\u0437 \u043e\u0442 \u043e\u0442\u0432\u0435\u0442\u0441\u0442\u0432\u0435\u043d\u043d\u043e\u0441\u0442\u0438:** \u041c\u043e\u0434 \u0441\u043e\u0437\u0434\u0430\u043d **\u0438\u0441\u043a\u043b\u044e\u0447\u0438\u0442\u0435\u043b\u044c\u043d\u043e \u0441 \u0446\u0435\u043b\u044c\u044e \u044f\u0437\u044b\u043a\u043e\u0432\u043e\u0439 \u0434\u043e\u0441\u0442\u0443\u043f\u043d\u043e\u0441\u0442\u0438** \u0438 \u043d\u0435 \u0441\u043e\u0434\u0435\u0440\u0436\u0438\u0442 \u0447\u0438\u0442\u043e\u0432, \u043f\u0440\u0435\u0438\u043c\u0443\u0449\u0435\u0441\u0442\u0432 \u0438\u043b\u0438 \u0438\u0437\u043c\u0435\u043d\u0435\u043d\u0438\u0439 \u0438\u0433\u0440\u043e\u0432\u043e\u0433\u043e \u043f\u0440\u043e\u0446\u0435\u0441\u0441\u0430. \u041e\u0434\u043d\u0430\u043a\u043e \u0430\u0432\u0442\u043e\u0440\u044b \u0440\u0443\u0441\u0438\u0444\u0438\u043a\u0430\u0442\u043e\u0440\u0430 **\u043d\u0435 \u043d\u0435\u0441\u0443\u0442 \u043e\u0442\u0432\u0435\u0442\u0441\u0442\u0432\u0435\u043d\u043d\u043e\u0441\u0442\u0438** \u0437\u0430 \u043b\u044e\u0431\u044b\u0435 \u0441\u0430\u043d\u043a\u0446\u0438\u0438, \u0434\u0438\u0441\u043a\u0432\u0430\u043b\u0438\u0444\u0438\u043a\u0430\u0446\u0438\u0438 \u0438\u043b\u0438 \u0431\u043b\u043e\u043a\u0438\u0440\u043e\u0432\u043a\u0438 (\u0431\u0430\u043d\u044b), \u043a\u043e\u0442\u043e\u0440\u044b\u0435 \u043c\u043e\u0433\u0443\u0442 \u0431\u044b\u0442\u044c \u043d\u0430\u043b\u043e\u0436\u0435\u043d\u044b \u0430\u0434\u043c\u0438\u043d\u0438\u0441\u0442\u0440\u0430\u0446\u0438\u0435\u0439 \u0441\u0435\u0440\u0432\u0435\u0440\u043e\u0432 Draftout \u043f\u0440\u0438 \u0438\u0433\u0440\u0435 \u0432 \u0441\u043e\u0440\u0435\u0432\u043d\u043e\u0432\u0430\u0442\u0435\u043b\u044c\u043d\u043e\u043c \u0440\u0435\u0436\u0438\u043c\u0435 (Competitive). \u0418\u0441\u043f\u043e\u043b\u044c\u0437\u0443\u0439\u0442\u0435 \u043d\u0430 \u0441\u0432\u043e\u0439 \u0441\u0442\u0440\u0430\u0445 \u0438 \u0440\u0438\u0441\u043a.\n- \u0412 \u043a\u0430\u0437\u0443\u0430\u043b\u044c\u043d\u044b\u0445 \u0440\u0435\u0436\u0438\u043c\u0430\u0445 \u0438 \u043f\u0440\u0438\u0432\u0430\u0442\u043d\u044b\u0445 \u043b\u043e\u0431\u0431\u0438 \u043f\u0440\u0430\u0432\u0438\u043b\u0430 \u0443\u0441\u0442\u0430\u043d\u0430\u0432\u043b\u0438\u0432\u0430\u044e\u0442\u0441\u044f \u0441\u043e\u0437\u0434\u0430\u0442\u0435\u043b\u0435\u043c \u043a\u043e\u043c\u043d\u0430\u0442\u044b.\n\n</details>\n\n---\n\n## \ud83d\udcd6 About the Mod\n\n**The Draftout Russifier** is a standalone Fabric localization mod that brings full, high-quality Russian language support to the competitive Minecraft mod **[Draftout](https://modrinth.com/mod/draftout)**.\n\n### \u2753 Why a mod instead of a resource pack?\nIn the Draftout mod, custom user resource packs are automatically stripped during matches (`PackRepositoryMixin`). This mod integrates the Russian localization directly into the game's client environment, ensuring all board goals, lobbies, replay controls, and UI elements stay fully translated in Russian even during active matches.\n\n---\n\n## \u2728 Features (639 Translated Keys)\n\n- **All Bingo Goals:** Precise translations for all board objectives (advancements, mob interactions, breeding, unique crafts, potions, combat damage, and survival challenges) matching official Minecraft Russian terminology.\n- **Lobbies & Leaderboard:** Clean translation for lobby creation, timers, overtime, board parameters, and ranking screens.\n- **In-Game Translation Editor:** Customize or tweak any string directly in-game from the main menu with hot-reload and persistent config storage.\n- **Board Builder:** Complete localization of hints, board name inputs, search filters, saving, and loading features.\n- **Replay System:** Fully translated replay controls, player-following shortcuts, seek actions, and goal completion navigation.\n- **Settings & Preferences:** Board positioning, scaling, goal completion opacity, and utility options.\n\n---\n\n## Installation\n\n1. Make sure you have **Fabric Loader** installed for Minecraft **26.1.1**.\n2. Install the original **[Draftout](https://modrinth.com/mod/draftout)**\n3. Download **The Draftout Russifier**\n4. Launch the game and set your language to **\u0420\u0443\u0441\u0441\u043a\u0438\u0439 (\u0420\u043e\u0441\u0441\u0438\u044f)** in the Minecraft Language Settings.\n\n---\n\n## \u26a0\ufe0f Important Disclaimer & Draftout Rules\n\nPlease review the [official Draftout rules (Section 03: Mod rules)](https://draftoutmc.com/rules#mods) before participating in competitive gameplay:\n\n- **Unofficial Project:** This translation mod is **NOT officially endorsed, approved, or maintained by the Draftout development or moderation team**.\n- **Disclaimer of Liability:** This project is created **solely for accessibility and language translation**. It does not alter game mechanics, provide cheats, or give any gameplay advantages. However, the authors and contributors **assume no responsibility** for any potential warnings, match disqualifications, or account bans on official Draftout competitive servers. Use at your own discretion.\n- In private lobbies and casual games, rules are determined by the lobby host.", "body_url": null, "published": "2026-08-18T20:23:07.437235Z", "updated": "2026-08-21T12:37:07.387185Z", "approved": "2026-09-24T18:51:33.224986Z", "queued": "2026-08-18T21:10:08.802306Z", "status": "approved", "requested_status": "approved", "moderator_message": null, "license": {"id": "CC0-1.0", "name": "Creative Commons Zero v1.0 Universal", "url": "https://github.com/MjKey/RuOut/blob/main/LICENSE"}, "downloads": 2, "followers": 0, "categories": ["utility"], "additional_categories": [], "loaders": ["fabric"], "versions": ["fuFnG2MP", "BNjxz13J", "7MyjzKWT"], "icon_url": "https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/clgug7NI/fa8d0bb06cc2415dc9e609e9393d3a9d91cb433a.png", "raw_icon_url": "https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/clgug7NI/fa8d0bb06cc2415dc9e609e9393d3a9d91cb433a.png", "issues_url": "https://github.com/MjKey/RuOut/issues", "source_url": "https://github.com/MjKey/RuOut", "wiki_url": null, "discord_url": null, "donation_urls": [], "gallery": [{"url": "https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/clgug7NI/images/4124e9fafc7836bb1bbc7492337a8b01a804b8d7_350.webp", "raw_url": "https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/clgug7NI/images/4124e9fafc7836bb1bbc7492337a8b01a804b8d7.png", "featured": false, "title": null, "description": null, "created": "2026-08-18T21:03:47.096055Z", "ordering": 0}, {"url": "https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/clgug7NI/images/775bdbd6606c5a5b4fa2e510d8411916979cb56e_350.webp", "raw_url": "https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/clgug7NI/images/775bdbd6606c5a5b4fa2e510d8411916979cb56e.png", "featured": false, "title": null, "description": null, "created": "2026-08-18T21:05:23.566977Z", "ordering": 0}], "color": 4411473, "thread_id": "Y27ZyDFv", "monetization_status": "demonetized"}, {"client_side": "required", "server_side": "required", "game_versions": ["1.20.1"], "environment": ["client_and_server"], "id": "zpirRH8N", "slug": "izaryas-pocket-dimension", "project_type": "mod", "team": "9cVPbJ6J", "organization": null, "title": "Pocket Dimension", "description": "Adds a 1000x1000 pocket dimension that can be accessed anywhere with a Dimensional Sack. Pocket dimension is shared across all players.", "body": "- Adds a new dimension to the game that can be accessed by holding right-click with the Dimensional Sack in hand.\n- The Pocket Dimension is 1000x256x1000 blocks with barrier blocks on all four sides and a ceiling.\n- Made up of nothing but a single flat layer of an unbreakable material.\n- Your position is saved when entering and exiting the Pocket Dimension.\n- Can be accessed from any position in any dimension.\n- Currently, the Pocket Dimension is shared between all players.", "body_url": null, "published": "2026-08-19T04:31:08.518905Z", "updated": "2026-08-19T04:57:47.329518Z", "approved": "2026-09-24T19:32:13.829395Z", "queued": "2026-08-19T04:59:16.305176Z", "status": "approved", "requested_status": "approved", "moderator_message": null, "license": {"id": "MIT", "name": "MIT License", "url": null}, "downloads": 1, "followers": 0, "categories": ["storage", "utility", "worldgen"], "additional_categories": ["management"], "loaders": ["forge"], "versions": ["dMPOHJJy"], "icon_url": "https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/zpirRH8N/9c1409d316bedf33e6174aca6d9d0595b037258d.png", "raw_icon_url": "https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/zpirRH8N/9c1409d316bedf33e6174aca6d9d0595b037258d.png", "issues_url": null, "source_url": null, "wiki_url": null, "discord_url": null, "donation_urls": [], "gallery": [{"url": "https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/zpirRH8N/images/9c1409d316bedf33e6174aca6d9d0595b037258d.png", "raw_url": "https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/zpirRH8N/images/9c1409d316bedf33e6174aca6d9d0595b037258d.png", "featured": false, "title": "The Dimensional Sack", "description": "Hold right-click while in hand to teleport to the Pocket Dimension.", "created": "2026-08-19T04:39:39.516438Z", "ordering": 1}, {"url": "https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/zpirRH8N/images/e814adc75b7a8fb733481c20e408e2eaef905c42.png", "raw_url": "https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/zpirRH8N/images/e814adc75b7a8fb733481c20e408e2eaef905c42.png", "featured": false, "title": "Dimensional Sack Crafting Recipe", "description": null, "created": "2026-08-19T04:40:02.599754Z", "ordering": 2}, {"url": "https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/zpirRH8N/images/44cc96965b2fc76097f32c32d8f1b50862928529_350.webp", "raw_url": "https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/zpirRH8N/images/44cc96965b2fc76097f32c32d8f1b50862928529.png", "featured": true, "title": "The Pocket Dimension", "description": "Nothing but a flat, open space. You're limited to a 1000x1000 block area.", "created": "2026-08-19T04:41:46.702805Z", "ordering": 3}], "color": 6960740, "thread_id": "jTEbCzIW", "monetization_status": "monetized"}, {"client_side": "required", "server_side": "unsupported", "game_versions": ["1.20", "1.20.1", "1.20.2", "1.20.3", "1.20.4", "1.20.5", "1.20.6", "1.21", "1.21.1", "1.21.2", "1.21.3", "1.21.4", "1.21.5", "1.21.6", "1.21.7", "1.21.8", "1.21.9", "1.21.10", "1.21.11", "26.1", "26.1.1", "26.1.2", "26.2"], "environment": ["client_only"], "id": "RWtUJXS3", "slug": "evatex-background-video", "project_type": "mod", "team": "MQzchR52", "organization": null, "title": "EVATEX-Background Video", "description": "Replaces the Minecraft main menu background with your own video. Pick any video from the in-game Video Menu \u2014 just drop files into the videos folder.", "body": "# \ud83c\udfac EVATEX-Background Video\n\n**Replace Minecraft's boring main menu panorama with your own video!** \ud83c\udfae\u2728\n\nEvery time you reach the main menu, your video plays in the background \u2014 your favorite clip, an animation, a looping cinematic, a stream intro... whatever you want. All you have to do is drop a video into the `videos` folder and the mod does the rest. **Made by EverVerity.** \ud83d\udc9c\n\n---\n\n## \u2728 Features\n\n- \ud83d\uddbc\ufe0f **Your video, your main menu** \u2014 plays MP4, MOV, WebM, MKV, AVI and more instead of the panorama\n- \ud83d\udce6 **Zero setup, no installs:** FFmpeg is bundled inside the mod \u2014 just drop the jar into `mods` and play\n- \ud83c\udf9b\ufe0f **Full control:** pick your video, adjust scale, FPS, darkening and vignette\n- \ud83d\udcc2 **Easy management:** everything is configured in-game via the \"Video Menu\" button\n- \ud83d\udd04 **Multi-version support:** works on Minecraft **1.20 and above**\n- \ud83d\udee1\ufe0f **Safe:** on an unsupported version the mod silently disables itself \u2014 the game never crashes\n- \u26a1 **Lightweight:** only active on the main menu, never interferes with gameplay\n\n---\n\n## \ud83d\udce5 Installation\n\n1. Install **Fabric Loader** and **Fabric API** (easy with Fabric's own installer)\n2. Drop the mod's `.jar` file into the `mods` folder of your game directory\n3. Launch the game \u2014 **that's it!** \ud83c\udf89\n\n> \u2705 **Nothing to install.** The mod ships with its own FFmpeg build for **Windows** and **Linux** \u2014 no FFmpeg, no dependencies, no command line. Just drop the jar into `mods` and run.\n\n---\n\n## \ud83d\ude80 How to Use\n\n### 1\ufe0f\u20e3 Add Videos\nDrop your videos into the `videos` folder inside your game directory:\n\n- \ud83d\udcc1 Locate your game folder (`.../.minecraft/` or your launcher's folder)\n- \ud83d\udcfd\ufe0f Copy your videos into the `videos` folder\n- \u2705 Supported formats: **MP4, MOV, WebM, MKV, AVI, M4V** and any other format FFmpeg supports\n- \ud83d\udca1 **Tip:** looping videos or short showcase clips give the best results\n\n### 2\ufe0f\u20e3 Select a Video\n- Click the **\"Video Menu\"** button in the top-right corner of the main menu\n- Pick the video you want \u2014 the background updates instantly\n\n### 3\ufe0f\u20e3 Adjust Settings\nFrom the Video Menu you can tweak the following:\n\n| Setting | What it does |\n|---------|--------------|\n| \ud83c\udf9e\ufe0f **Video** | Switch between videos in the `videos` folder |\n| \ud83d\udd0d **Scale** | Fitting mode for the video (fit, stretch, etc.) |\n| \u23f1\ufe0f **FPS** | Frame rate \u2014 lower FPS means less CPU usage |\n| \ud83c\udf11 **Darkening** | Darkens the background so buttons are easier to read |\n| \ud83c\udf47 **Vignette** | Toggles the edge darkening effect |\n| \ud83d\udcc1 **Open Videos** | Opens the `videos` folder in your file manager |\n\nYour settings are saved automatically \u2014 they are applied on the next launch as well. \ud83d\udd01\n\n---\n\n## \ud83d\udee0\ufe0f Requirements\n\n- \ud83c\udfae Minecraft **1.20 and above** (client)\n- \ud83e\uddf5 Fabric Loader (`>= 0.16.0`)\n- \ud83d\udce6 Fabric API\n- \u2615 Java 21\n- \ud83c\udfa5 **FFmpeg** \u2014 already bundled with the mod (Windows & Linux). No installation needed.\n\n---\n\n## \ud83d\udd27 Troubleshooting\n\n| Problem | Solution |\n|---------|----------|\n| Video not playing | Make sure the file in `videos` is a supported format (MP4/H.264 recommended) |\n| Video too fast/slow | Change the FPS setting from the Video Menu |\n| Buttons hard to read | Turn on the Darkening setting |\n| Mod not visible | Check that the jar is in `mods` and you launched the game with Fabric |\n\n---\n\n## \ud83d\udcdc License\n\nThis mod is licensed under the **MIT** license. EverVerity \u00a9 2026. \ud83d\udc9c\n\nThe mod bundles statically-linked builds of **FFmpeg** (GPL v3) for Windows and Linux. FFmpeg is a free software project created by the FFmpeg developers (https://ffmpeg.org); the source code is available from the build maintainers we used (https://github.com/BtbN/FFmpeg-Builds and https://www.gyan.dev/ffmpeg/builds/). A copy of the GNU GPL v3 is included inside the jar (`assets/videomenu/ffmpeg/COPYING.GPLv3`).\n\n---\n\n*Make the main menu yours again \u2014 your video is right there, waiting for you. \ud83c\udfac\u2728*\n", "body_url": null, "published": "2026-08-12T05:06:40.538674Z", "updated": "2026-08-12T08:11:15.641638Z", "approved": "2026-09-24T17:51:54.283619Z", "queued": "2026-08-12T05:55:37.368725Z", "status": "approved", "requested_status": "approved", "moderator_message": null, "license": {"id": "MIT", "name": "MIT License", "url": null}, "downloads": 7, "followers": 2, "categories": ["management", "technology", "utility"], "additional_categories": [], "loaders": ["fabric"], "versions": ["K13nHzsW", "uUuz5yJq", "kualdgen", "aW88Gu2P"], "icon_url": "https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/RWtUJXS3/df89b8a59d8804e1f10a9bc334491ca9d3bc8774_96.webp", "raw_icon_url": "https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/RWtUJXS3/df89b8a59d8804e1f10a9bc334491ca9d3bc8774.png", "issues_url": null, "source_url": "https://github.com/ZeninKaanX/evatex-background-video-1.6.0", "wiki_url": null, "discord_url": null, "donation_urls": [], "gallery": [{"url": "https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/RWtUJXS3/images/01ea541c664391f9314e41e83edd9a19eeed6424_350.webp", "raw_url": "https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/RWtUJXS3/images/01ea541c664391f9314e41e83edd9a19eeed6424.png", "featured": false, "title": "You can edit background", "description": null, "created": "2026-08-12T05:21:13.248269Z", "ordering": 0}, {"url": "https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/RWtUJXS3/images/18132879d136a7ddc823fc2198760440ab22b5b3_350.webp", "raw_url": "https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/RWtUJXS3/images/18132879d136a7ddc823fc2198760440ab22b5b3.png", "featured": false, "title": "mod menu ", "description": null, "created": "2026-08-12T05:21:32.721333Z", "ordering": 0}], "color": 13805224, "thread_id": "dTBUeAZ0", "monetization_status": "monetized"}, {"client_side": "required", "server_side": "unsupported", "game_versions": ["26.2"], "environment": ["client_only"], "id": "ElXoFoVv", "slug": "aechronis-essentials", "project_type": "mod", "team": "2l62XeG1", "organization": null, "title": "Aechronis Essentials", "description": "Certain useful features for the Minecraft server Aechronis, including coloring hitboxes based on diplomacy state.", "body": "# Aechronis Essentials\n\nColors players hitboxes based off of live data from the Aechronis server\n\nClient-side only. Inert unless you're actually connected to an Aechronis server.\n\n## Features\n\n- **Auto relation coloring** : player hitboxes are colored automatically based on town/nation/ally/enemy standing, using live data from Aechronis's Nodes map.\n- **Chunk border recoloring (F3+G)** : the debug chunk grid is tinted by territory ownership the same way, so you can read who owns the land around you at a glance.\n- **Manual override lists** : keep your own friend/enemy name lists that take priority over auto-detected relations.\n- **Auto `/t spawn` on respawn** : optional quality-of-life toggle that sends you back to town spawn automatically when you die.\n\n## Requirements\n\n- Minecraft 26.2 (Java 25)\n- Fabric Loader \u2265 0.19.3\n- Fabric API\n- Cloth Config\n- Mod Menu (recommended, for in-game settings)\n\n## Notes\n\n- This mod only activates when connected to an official Aechronis server \u2014 it does nothing on other servers.\n- Colors and opacity for every category are fully configurable through Mod Menu / Cloth Config.\n\n## Links\n- Discord: https://discord.gg/A3sSsZKuw8\n- GitHub: https://github.com/DCFiendish/Aechronis-Essentials\n\n## Credits\n\nHitbox-coloring logic is a from-source GPLv3 port of the equivalent feature in [CrusalisUtils](https://github.com/oreotrollturbo/Crusalis-utils-) by oreotrollturbo, retargeted from Crusalis's Dynmap/Towny data to Aechronis's Nodes map API and rebuilt against Minecraft 26.2's Gizmos-based debug renderer.\n\nLicensed under GPL-3.0-or-later.\n", "body_url": null, "published": "2026-